WEBVTT

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.250
Car 4 stabilisation complete.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.050
Roger.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.270
This is car 2. Stabilisation complete.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.960
Roger, car 2.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.840
Car 3 is stabilised.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.210
Car 1 is ready!

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.020
Roger.

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.920
Inspector! All cars are in position!

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:53.440
Infiltration Squad{***is this the best title?}, what's happening inside?

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.600
As you said, all the security is down.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.990
How about the diamond?

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.870
It's gone. The case was broken open.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.600
This is Team B.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.730
Target has not entered the first floor emergency stairs.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.250
We're heading up now.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.860
Don't worry about keeping a low profile.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.030
Chase him all the way up!

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.070
Roger!

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.260
Okay, let's go over the plan one last time.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:21.260
No matter where he tries to escape from, the four jet turbines will blow him into Tsukishima River.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.000
Then we'll scoop him up like a goldfish at a funfair.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.500
Today's the day he's not getting away!

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.800
Will he really just let himself be blown by the wind?

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.270
What if he attacks with his card gun?

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.340
His pseudo-bullets may be tough, but they're still cards.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.780
The wind'll take care of them.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.060
He turns his cape into a kite and fires cards…

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.980
As cool as he makes himself out to be, he's got no chance against the wind!

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.790
Kid! Kid! Kid! Kid! Kid!

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.710
Inspector!

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.910
So you finally show yourself, Kid!

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.340
All units, get into position!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:58.930
Sir!

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.270
I'll be taking this little diamond.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.520
Who's he supposed to be?

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.030
Begin Operation ‘Catch Kid’!

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.150
All cars, start your turbines!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.110
Kid's heading East!

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.250
Cars 2 and 4, pattern B!

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.390
We've got him!

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.500
Oh, Kid!

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.560
Can't even open your kite out of shock, huh?

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.060
50 metres to Tsukishima River!

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:54.060
Tsukishima River Capture Squad, wind up the net!{***is this the best title?}

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.900
Kid fired a gun! Kid fired a gun!

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.420
Kid used a <i>gun</i>?!

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.160
Kid's escaping in a houseboat!

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.870
He's heading up Tsukishima River!

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.410
Where's the helicopters?!

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.830
This plan didn't call for any helicopters…

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:30.850
{nakamori}Kid… fired a <i>gun</i>?!

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.850
{background character}All we have is a water police boat!

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.060
Damn it!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.600
Why's this huge net here?!

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.360
We can't follow him!

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.360
Stop, Kid!

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.550
You won't get away!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.350
Guess that's not enough to get rid of him…

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.310
The Zantetsuken…?{TL note: Steel-Cleaving Sword}

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:56.910
Now I get it…

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.820
You should've just told me that in the first place…

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.430
Lupin III!

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.900
This is Lupin III.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:30.930
An elusive thief who never misses
 a heist as he travels the world.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.950
His partners are Daisuke Jigen…

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.900
A professional sharpshooter
 who can quick draw in 0.3 seconds.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.620
{A duty-bound and cool gunman.Typeset: Don't call me <red>DADDY <anger>!</red>}A cool gunman with a strong sense of duty.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.030
And Goemon Ishikawa XIII…

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:47.880
A master of <i>iai</i>-swordplay who can cleave anything in half.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.760
A man you wouldn't want to get angry.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.060
And let's not forget…

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.060
Fujiko Mine, a mysterious lady.

00:06:58.730 --> 00:07:02.420
Even Lupin can't work out whether she's a thief or a spy.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.710
She always puts him through the wringer…

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.630
Makes me wonder why he puts up with her!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.180
Because Lupin can't resist cute girls.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:11.320
Apparently.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.540
This is Shin'ichi Kudō, a high-school detective.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:25.380
When he went to a theme park with a childhood friend and classmate, Ran Mouri,

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:30.370
he happened to see a dangerous
 deal between some scary guys in black…

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.010
But while he was focused on them…

00:07:33.010 --> 00:07:37.160
He didn't notice they had another partner sneaking up on him from behind, see?

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.640
That guy forced him to swallow poison, and when he came to…

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.630
What a shock!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:45.340
Somehow, his body had shrunk!

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:53.010
And so, if those guys figured Shin'ichi Kudō was still alive, they'd come back to finish him off and put everyone he knows in danger.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:57.580
So Shin'ichi Kudō decided to hide his
identity and call himself Conan Edogawa,

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:03.110
and ended up living with a girl
 named Ran and her detective dad.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.800
Never mind! I'll just ask Kid-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.570
K-Kid-<i>sama</i>?!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:11.920
Why, Kaitō Kid.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:12.740
Haven't you heard of him?

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:13.910
Course I have!

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:18.870
They say he's the ‘Magician Under the Moonlight’ or something, but he's really just some high-schooler brat!

00:08:18.870 --> 00:08:20.420
Oh, that's just great!

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:21.880
So where is he?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.940
Where's his school? I'm begging you, Lupin!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.060
‘Kid-<i>sama</i>’ got the jewel, just like you wanted.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.770
Good evening, Lupin-<i>kun</i>…

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:40.200
That was quite the show you put on there…

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.310
If you already know, then that saves me explaining.

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:45.620
Disable the bomb, then.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.150
I can't do that.

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:49.320
What?

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:53.130
I have to see if you really <i>will</i> listen to me for her sake…

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.740
Whether I can really trust you.

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.140
A test?

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.620
I apologise.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:02.030
A certain man gave you the highest recommendation…

00:09:02.030 --> 00:09:07.150
He said the only thief who could steal the Cherry Sapphire was Lupin III — in other words, you.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.960
Glad to hear it.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:11.650
So, does this mean I passed the test?

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.050
Of course.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.550
Well then, contact me once you have the Cherry Sapphire.

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:21.020
I'll disable her bomb then.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:22.830
Oh, and that's right…

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:27.110
Trying to trace this number would just be a waste of time.

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.610
Sounds about right.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.210
By the way, where does it look like I'm calling from?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:36.720
It was up in the mountains of China until a moment ago, but now it's coming from a satellite above America.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.280
I give up, I give up…

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:39.590
I admit it…

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.100
You're an enemy I have to take seriously.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:49.100
I must never forget that I'm dealing with Lupin III either.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:10.250
It's split right through…

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.920
How'd it get cut like this?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.530
Even the bulletproof carbon inside was cut through…{***}

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.420
How terrifying…

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:22.500
Looks like this one's better for you after all.

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.790
Why would he go through all the trouble of stealing it, just to throw it in a bucket?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.430
I just can't understand it.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:29.540
Maybe he just simply wanted to cause some mayhem?

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:35.180
In the end, even with everyone trying to catch him, all they caught were three fish in the net. They just weren't prepared at all.

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.660
Conan-<i>kun</i>'s just watching TV…

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:36.900
He doesn't look happy…

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.810
It's because he always tries to do everything himself.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.200
It was some guy called Goemon that beat him, right?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.310
On various sites, people are saying that Lupin III has been spotted in Japan.

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:50.690
Goemon's one of Lupin's pals, right?

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:52.630
Then he's in this city?

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.780
Well then, time for the quiz you've been waiting for!

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:56.530
Huh?!

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.550
Another pun quiz…?

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.240
I'm not really in the mood…

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.260
We haven't been waiting for one.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.270
Hey… Help me out here.

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.500
We can't get started without a good quiz, can we?!

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:11.250
We've been really excited!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.770
I wonder if I can solve it!

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.770
How obvious can you get…{Conan}

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:19.340
Today, I've even got a board ready!

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.360
I've been waiting for this!

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:25.100
You're the best, Doctor!

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.560
Look over here!

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:27.790
I'm looking!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:32.040
One of these four beans is loved by Lupin.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.040
So, can you work out which one?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.670
I'll give you five minutes to think it over.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.920
FIVE MINUTES LATER

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.800
Now, have you figured it out?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:41.780
That was quick!

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:44.830
They're all the same if you eat them…

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.370
Genta-<i>kun</i>…

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:49.060
You should've <i>bean</i> thinking harder about this.{mame vs mame pun, 'bean' vs 'carefully'}

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:51.580
The answer is number 3, broad beans.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:53.440
Oh, why's that?

00:11:53.440 --> 00:12:01.050
sansei

00:11:53.440 --> 00:12:01.050
The rest are all alkaline, but broad beans are acidic, right?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.680
Acidic?

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:03.850
So?

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:07.490
Lupin…

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.660
sansei

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:09.660
The Third!

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.250
Hurray! Hurray! Hurray!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.170
Are you looking for a fight?

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:19.170
This morning, Emilio Barretti, a popular Italian idol, arrived in Japan.{***check surname}

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:22.320
He travels the world…

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.180
I had no idea I'd see <i>him</i> again…

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:30.290
Wow! Emilio's doing a concert in Japan! Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.000
The Prince of Music, Emilio Barretti!{young noble is onscreen later}

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:35.190
Even in Japan, he's very popular!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.920
There he is, that's my brother.{***}

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:37.690
Where?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.970
Did you see her?

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.180
I did.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:42.890
Isn't she pretty?

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.510
She is.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:46.700
Maybe she's his manager?

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.230
What a pretty lady!

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:50.200
Yeah!

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.480
They may be boys, but they're definitely men.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:56.770
They still can't take their eyes off a pretty lady.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.460
No comments here.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:03.620
And that was our footage from Haneda.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:06.720
You can really tell that a great star has arrived.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.490
There's no mistaking that man…

00:13:08.490 --> 00:13:10.500
That was Daisuke Jigen!

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:15.290
Oh, even Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:17.090
H-Huh? What? N-No!

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.590
He's the worst, isn't he?

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:20.470
Unbelievable!

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:20.470
Guys!

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.730
You were staring at her!

00:13:20.970 --> 00:13:22.730
I wasn't!

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.180
This is the diamond he mistakenly stole.

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.230
And these are the bullets he shot into the crane.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:35.730
Mistakenly… He makes mistakes like that?

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:37.000
That's just Lupin.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:43.760
Disguising as Kid, stealing a diamond he didn't want, and throwing it into a fisherman's bucket…

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:47.630
These are all signs of him setting us a challenge.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:49.620
A challenge!

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:51.890
But that isn't the case.

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:56.420
He's just joking around, right, Inspector Zenigata?

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.060
Yeah…

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:01.050
What he's after this time is a jewel called the Cherry Sapphire.

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:01.050
The ICPO?!

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:03.260
I see you've met him before, Takagi-<i>kun</i>.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.700
The only agent in the whole ICPO assigned solely to Lupin III.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.390
Nice to meet you.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:10.450
I'm Zenigata.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:14.190
Inspector, does Lupin always play jokes like that?

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.480
He does.

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:18.560
Maybe we're better off not overthinking things.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:22.710
Then how can we tell that he's really after the Cherry Sapphire?

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.420
Right! What if it's another joke?

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:26.490
He sent me an e-mail.

00:14:26.910 --> 00:14:28.740
H-He sends you e-mails?!

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.620
He does.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:30.790
No replying, though.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.900
What sort of e-mails?

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:33.660
Take a look.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:36.040
Let me see, let me see!

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.470
Hey, calm down…

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.750
Inspector Megure!

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.850
Can I borrow some of these agents of yours?

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:44.550
I don't mind, but I don't know if they'll be of any help…

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:45.930
I'll help!

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.820
Can I join the Lupin investigation?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:54.990
It'd usually be under Investigation Division Two's jurisdiction, but Inspector Nakamori's been given a forced vacation.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:58.100
No surprise after the mess at Tsukishima.

00:14:58.100 --> 00:14:58.830
Then…

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:02.070
Just this once, you can take several officers from Division One.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.830
Take me, me, me, me!

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.570
M-Me too!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.340
I never thought I'd get a chance to help arrest Lupin.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.040
Right, Lupin III was your first love, Satō-<i>san</i>.

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.350
Takagi-<i>kun</i>…

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:16.500
I see…

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.460
You want to get your hands on him before anyone else…

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:19.710
It's not like that.

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:22.340
I wouldn't have put myself forward for such a fickle reason…

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:23.860
Sounds fine to me…

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.840
Arresting your first love…

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.800
You won't want someone else to beat you to it.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.240
I expect great things from you.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.890
Inspector Zenigata…

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:37.240
I'll do my best!

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:41.250
You could say that I love Lupin too, in a way…

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.820
It's ridiculous, parking here of all places…

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:50.200
I'll show you what happens when you pick a fight with the Traffic Department.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.490
But why couldn't we find a match
 for the number plate, <i>Sempai</i>?

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:57.500
I guess it just means that it's no ordinary fake numberplate.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.390
Well, there are some pretty shady organisations around!

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.210
It's chock-full of suspicion!

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.210
Do people say ‘chock-full’ anymore?

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:05.900
Huh? They don't?

00:16:08.090 --> 00:16:11.390
You… parked here?

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.010
It was an Interpol car…

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:18.100
Our Traffic Department is relentless.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.270
The Miyamoto-Mi'ike duo, huh?

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:22.690
I'll go to the Traffic Department!

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.790
I wonder if there's a fine…

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.860
It's Sonoko.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:31.050
Hi, what is it?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:33.240
The TV? Now?

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:33.930
Welcome to Japan!

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.700
What's your favourite Japanese food?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.430
Yeah, I'm watching.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:36.430
<i>Nattō</i>.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:39.460
I'm going to see him tomorrow after school.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.460
{Ran: You can't mean…?}Yes! Emilio!

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.310
In person!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.310
I figured out what hotel he's staying at!

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:47.920
No way!

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.570
How'd you figure that out?

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:53.150
With my information network, it was a piece of cake.

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.560
Your information network?

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.660
But what about personal privacy?

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:01.020
That's fine… Okay.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.650
We'll meet there, right?

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:05.670
Okay. Right, see you tomorrow.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.690
Wow! His manager's beautiful too!

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:09.670
What are you saying?

00:17:09.670 --> 00:17:11.740
Oh, I can't believe Sonoko…

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:14.530
Her homework could've waited until tomorrow…

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.430
You're going to see Emilio, right?

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.420
Geez…

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:20.870
Pretty pretty lady!

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:22.930
The old man's just as bad as the kids…

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.580
I'm coming too!

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:25.920
What?!

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:35.700
Do we really need things like <i>that</i>?

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.890
He often escapes by helicopter.

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:40.580
Often…?! You mean you'd shoot him down?!

00:17:41.050 --> 00:17:43.560
Will this really be all right?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.980
Maybe we should've moved it after all…

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.330
It's to our advantage that it stays here.

00:17:49.650 --> 00:17:53.910
If we were to move it, we'd just be giving Lupin a chance, after all.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:54.880
I agree.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.070
Both of you, come with me to the safe room.

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:57.830
Right!

00:17:57.830 --> 00:17:58.910
M-Me too?

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.640
Wow… that's some vault.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.580
Have you contacted the Sapphire's owner?

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:14.880
Yes. I asked him whether he would like it moved,
even temporarily, but Eishin Wakagomo-<i>sama</i> said…

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:16.220
There's no need.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:19.030
I trust the Japanese police.

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:21.890
Looks like you've got a lot of trust riding on this.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:25.650
We'll catch him for sure!

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:26.980
You can leave it to us!

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:27.940
Right, Satō-<i>san</i>?

00:18:28.260 --> 00:18:29.210
Hey!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:31.290
Everyone! Let's work together and give it all we've got!

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:33.570
Yeah!

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:36.050
You're embarrassing us, just stay still!

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.030
Five minutes to Lupin's stated theft time!

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.030
‘Under Special Guard’

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.910
All roads have been sealed!

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.260
Vehicles will no longer be allowed through!

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:48.540
All officers but the specialist squad inside the bank are to switch to channel B!

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:56.180
Has Lupin ever been late before?

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.030
Never.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.840
Which means…

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.390
There's only one more minute…

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:03.030
So he has to be somewhere nearby.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.980
Yeah. He might even be in here, disguised as one of us.

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:07.790
What?!

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.650
B-But who?!

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:12.150
Stop, Satō-<i>san</i>!

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:12.880
Don't move!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:13.940
I'll shoot!

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:16.900
He might not even be disguised as a person.

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.910
H-H-He can disguise himself…

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.490
…as other things?!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:25.470
What if that door itself was Lupin, in disguise?

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.210
Sorry.

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:35.020
I thought it might relieve some tension.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.530
Thought it might put smiles on your faces.

00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:42.070
It's already past 1 PM!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.640
N-Nothing's happened…

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:47.790
Maybe he changed his plans due to the high security?

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.960
He always steals his target.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.500
That's just how Lupin III is.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:58.150
Which means that Lupin is already in the vault…?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.700
You've seen it in movies, right?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.910
Thieves digging a tunnel under a bank vault to steal something.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:06.390
Are there cameras inside?

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.020
The safe-deposit boxes are private, so…

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:13.270
Let's take a look, just to be sure.

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:23.510
There's no hole, it seems.

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:24.780
Phew…

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:28.810
But what if the Cherry Sapphire alone was already…

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:30.660
What if it was already stolen?

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.810
N-No!

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.080
It couldn't be!

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.610
Do you have both of the keys?

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:38.400
Yes.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.300
Eishin-<i>sama</i> entrusted me with his key.

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.790
It's here.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.430
The Cherry Sapphire is safe.

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:57.050
It's already three minutes after his stated theft time.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:00.380
What if… What if…

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:05.240
…all of your watches were moved forward by three minutes?

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.220
What?!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.600
It's 1 PM now!

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.310
So that's it! Back then…

00:21:10.310 --> 00:21:15.560
Disguised as Takagi-<i>kun</i>, you moved all our watches forward by three minutes!

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:17.290
That's right, that's right, exactly right!

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.080
Right on time!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.710
I'll be takin' this, Pops.

00:21:30.710 --> 00:21:33.600
Having some downtime will do you the world of good.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.560
Farewell, my first love!

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:45.650
Ow, ow, ow! You'll break it! You'll break it!

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.530
You just had to go and stick to your promise.

00:21:50.270 --> 00:21:53.640
You should be glad it was a cute girl who caught you, and not me!

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:55.870
That's cheating, Pops!

00:21:55.870 --> 00:22:00.180
You're using my maxim of never hitting a woman against me…

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:03.030
Let's see… Rewind three minutes…

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:08.050
Lupin III, at 13:02, I hereby arrest you red-handed for theft!

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.290
How brilliant!

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:13.120
Your talents are wasted at the rank of detective.

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:16.640
Sorry to butt in when you're celebrating, but…

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:17.880
Yes?

00:22:17.880 --> 00:22:19.800
There's not gonna be a warning shot,
 if you're planning to escape.

00:22:19.800 --> 00:22:21.050
Lupin!

00:22:21.050 --> 00:22:22.820
She's scary, you know?

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:27.150
I stuck silver stickers on the back of your watches.

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:28.760
Are they still there?

00:22:28.760 --> 00:22:30.220
Stickers?

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:32.140
Yes, but what for…?

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:36.940
Lupin-brand Shock Stickers!

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:39.290
They might be even stronger than a stun gun!

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:41.150
Sorry, missy!

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:42.790
You can have these back.

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:45.460
Wha-a-a?

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:47.820
You won't get away!

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:50.120
You can still stand, Pops?!

00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:51.490
Have another shock, on the house.

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:56.670
Sorry, missy!

00:22:56.670 --> 00:22:57.980
It wasn't me that got you involved in this!

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:00.100
Damn you!

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:01.670
Pops…

00:23:01.670 --> 00:23:04.050
You're not a zombie, you know?

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:06.630
If I shock you any more, that lady'll be in trouble.

00:23:06.630 --> 00:23:07.940
Bye-bye!

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:10.100
L-Lu-up-pi-in-n!

00:23:10.100 --> 00:23:10.700
Scary!

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:25.840
It's Lupin! He's in the safe room!

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.860
He's disguised as Inspector Zenigata!

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:30.470
Lupin!

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:30.590
There he is!

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:39.540
Right, right, in you get, in you get!

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:41.590
Idiots! It's not me!{timing starts late, should be before 'baaro!'}

00:23:41.590 --> 00:23:43.440
Ow-ow-ow! That's my face! My face!

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:45.340
Lupin spotted inside the bank!

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:46.470
Lupin…?

00:23:50.260 --> 00:23:53.030
It's Lupin!

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:55.520
This one's the real one!

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:59.440
Lupin #3, caught.

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:01.940
Lupin #4 spotted at a tobacconist!

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:05.540
We believe this one to be a fake…

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:06.690
We're a TV crew!

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:07.860
They won't come off!

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:10.920
They're too suspicious…

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:10.920
HQ, how can we tell which Lupin is the real one?!

00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:16.120
One canine Lupin spotted in Beika Park.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.110
He caught me.

00:24:18.110 --> 00:24:21.310
A squad of officers is in pursuit
 near the Beika Station North Exit!

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:23.460
I ran out of masks!

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:25.750
Lupin has entered Beika Street!

00:24:25.750 --> 00:24:27.760
Send officers in the south exit!

00:24:29.440 --> 00:24:31.490
Sorry to interrupt your shopping!

00:24:31.490 --> 00:24:33.360
Making money?

00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:36.290
Selling well?

00:24:36.290 --> 00:24:36.720
Eeesh!

00:24:36.720 --> 00:24:38.910
You should be saying ‘fish’{fish}, not ‘eeesh’!

00:24:38.910 --> 00:24:41.120
Take this! Squid! Octopus! Octopus ink!{***with stuff on screen, not much can be done}

00:24:41.120 --> 00:24:42.980
Get back! It's dangerous!

00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:43.610
The world can be cruel at times, right, Miss?{***}

00:24:42.980 --> 00:24:45.110
There's a dangerous criminal on the rampage!{***}

00:24:43.610 --> 00:24:44.690
How kind.

00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:47.360
mago

00:24:44.690 --> 00:24:47.360
You should meet my granddaughter{mago} sometime.

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:50.300
mago-mago

00:24:48.240 --> 00:24:50.300
Can't confuse{magomago} 'em forever!

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:57.290
Damn!

00:24:57.290 --> 00:24:59.760
They're playing right into his hands!

00:24:59.760 --> 00:25:01.170
What should we do?

00:25:01.170 --> 00:25:03.250
Send in more officers?

00:25:03.250 --> 00:25:04.460
The opposite!

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:06.090
Abandon the investigation.

00:25:06.750 --> 00:25:08.670
He's already gone.

00:25:08.670 --> 00:25:10.150
W-Where are you going?!

00:25:11.970 --> 00:25:14.140
My watch's all burnt…

00:25:14.140 --> 00:25:15.650
And it was my favourite…

00:25:16.680 --> 00:25:17.660
Huh?

00:25:17.660 --> 00:25:20.520
We've lost sight of Lupin!

00:25:27.920 --> 00:25:30.840
You really do need good legs to be a thief!

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:34.420
Always got another game of tag coming up…

00:25:39.700 --> 00:25:40.850
Don't tell me…

00:25:42.500 --> 00:25:46.560
If you couldn't use cars or helicopters…

00:25:46.560 --> 00:25:48.420
…you'd need to go to Beika Station…

00:25:48.420 --> 00:25:51.630
…but the station would be locked down straight away…

00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:56.570
The bank and the station would be too far apart…

00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.100
Even I agreed…

00:26:00.100 --> 00:26:01.270
Until I checked…

00:26:01.270 --> 00:26:04.370
…the locations of the ventilation shafts and maintenance entrances.

00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:07.560
That's good work, missy.

00:26:07.560 --> 00:26:09.000
I'll end up falling for you.

00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:10.900
But give me a break.

00:26:10.900 --> 00:26:13.000
I really need this.

00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:14.710
W-Wait…!

00:26:14.710 --> 00:26:17.780
When the shock wears off, let's play again sometime.

00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:24.750
That door…

00:26:24.750 --> 00:26:27.380
…leads to an access tunnel…

00:26:27.380 --> 00:26:29.350
…for electricity cables…

00:26:49.620 --> 00:26:52.630
A suspected rail accident just occurred, 
100 metres before reaching West Beika Station…

00:26:50.320 --> 00:26:51.230
Was that a person?

00:26:51.230 --> 00:26:52.630
Did they get hit?

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:59.030
Are you okay, Satō-<i>san</i>?!

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:02.140
Takagi-<i>kun</i>!

00:27:02.140 --> 00:27:04.580
I'm glad I made it in time…

00:27:04.580 --> 00:27:06.640
You mustn't be so reckless…

00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:10.790
That's a fine thing to say…

00:27:10.790 --> 00:27:15.480
You went and let Lupin catch you, right?

00:27:15.480 --> 00:27:18.010
Yes. And I'm sorry.

00:27:18.010 --> 00:27:19.360
I was careless.

00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:20.300
Hmph…

00:27:23.430 --> 00:27:27.700
I never want to leave your side again.

00:27:27.700 --> 00:27:29.560
That so?

00:27:30.230 --> 00:27:31.940
Huh?! Handcuffs?!

00:27:32.650 --> 00:27:34.360
You're Lupin, right?

00:27:34.360 --> 00:27:36.210
That's not like Takagi at all.

00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:38.960
Oh my, oh me, you noticed?

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:41.660
H-Hey! Wait!

00:27:41.660 --> 00:27:43.410
Lupin!

00:27:47.540 --> 00:27:48.580
What is it?

00:27:48.580 --> 00:27:51.210
Wasn't that Detective Satō's voice?

00:27:52.250 --> 00:27:53.520
You're hearing things!

00:27:53.520 --> 00:27:55.670
Sorry about having my dad here…

00:27:55.670 --> 00:28:00.640
It's fine! It'd be creepy if he was after Emilio, but it's his manager he's interested in, right?

00:28:00.640 --> 00:28:02.280
Even I could go for her.

00:28:02.280 --> 00:28:05.520
Now, we're here, Princess Ran!

00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:07.600
Give it up already!

00:28:09.980 --> 00:28:12.290
Being here feels so nostalgic…

00:28:12.290 --> 00:28:14.860
It hasn't even been that long!

00:28:14.860 --> 00:28:15.960
Right.

00:28:16.690 --> 00:28:19.360
You wait here, I'll go get a manager.

00:28:19.360 --> 00:28:20.960
You can just <i>do</i> that?

00:28:21.320 --> 00:28:28.120
I'm the detective who spectacularly foiled the poisoning of the Princess of Vespania — the Great Detective, Kogorō Mouri.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:30.000
What're you doing, Uncle?

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:32.080
My assistant made the arrangements.

00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:32.890
Assistant?

00:28:32.890 --> 00:28:34.960
Oh, what is he doing…

00:28:34.960 --> 00:28:37.550
Dad's not even supposed to be here…

00:28:37.550 --> 00:28:39.150
But it doesn't seem like it.

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:41.260
Oh, that's enough.

00:28:41.260 --> 00:28:43.640
Detective Mouri, I'll be glad to help,

00:28:43.640 --> 00:28:44.680
if you'd come this way…

00:28:44.680 --> 00:28:46.030
Oh, is that so!

00:28:46.030 --> 00:28:47.390
What's going on?

00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:48.890
What's going on?!

00:28:48.890 --> 00:28:50.190
What <i>is</i> going on?

00:28:50.190 --> 00:28:52.190
So what is going on?

00:28:52.860 --> 00:28:54.360
Let's go!

00:28:54.360 --> 00:28:55.320
What's it matter!

00:28:55.320 --> 00:28:56.710
Wait!

00:28:56.710 --> 00:28:58.900
So what if he's from Interpol?

00:28:58.900 --> 00:29:00.710
Breaking the law is breaking the law!

00:29:00.710 --> 00:29:04.410
No matter who he is, he's gonna pay the fine for being towed!

00:29:04.410 --> 00:29:06.590
It's precious money for the Treasury, after all!

00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:09.250
Should've come to get it himself!

00:29:09.250 --> 00:29:11.000
Maybe I'll leave him a nice big dent!

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:12.920
The key's inside, right?

00:29:12.920 --> 00:29:14.540
Behind the sun visor, apparently!

00:29:14.540 --> 00:29:15.710
Damn Westerners!

00:29:15.710 --> 00:29:16.840
<i>Sempai</i>!

00:29:16.840 --> 00:29:19.340
Takagi-<i>san</i>'s asleep on the back seats!

00:29:19.340 --> 00:29:19.800
What?

00:29:19.800 --> 00:29:20.730
Why?

00:29:20.730 --> 00:29:22.480
What're you doing?

00:29:22.480 --> 00:29:24.530
I was tied up!

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:29.830
Everybody's waiting in the conference room.

00:29:29.830 --> 00:29:32.120
My, waiting for me?

00:29:32.120 --> 00:29:34.120
I do apologise.

00:29:37.580 --> 00:29:40.110
Please turn left as you leave the lift.

00:29:40.110 --> 00:29:40.960
Right!

00:29:43.110 --> 00:29:44.570
It's this room here.

00:29:44.570 --> 00:29:46.030
My, this place does look familiar!

00:29:46.910 --> 00:29:48.410
Excuse me!

00:29:48.410 --> 00:29:49.720
Dad, you could at least knock!

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:51.000
So, how'd it go?

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:53.430
Oh, it's nothing.

00:29:53.950 --> 00:29:56.460
That's Inspector Shiratori!

00:29:57.230 --> 00:29:59.050
Mouri-<i>kun</i>?!

00:29:59.050 --> 00:30:00.020
Inspector?!

00:30:00.340 --> 00:30:01.840
Why are you here?

00:30:01.840 --> 00:30:02.930
Hello…

00:30:02.930 --> 00:30:03.780
Is he there? Is he there?!

00:30:03.780 --> 00:30:06.190
Megure-<i>san</i>, who are these people?

00:30:06.190 --> 00:30:08.320
Oh, don't worry. This is—

00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:13.980
The greatest detective in all of Japan,
Kogorō Mouri, at your service, <i>signorina</i>.

00:30:13.980 --> 00:30:15.620
R-Right…

00:30:16.730 --> 00:30:19.790
Please excuse him. I'm his daughter, Ran Mouri.

00:30:19.790 --> 00:30:22.280
And I'm his assistant, Sonoko Suzuki!

00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:23.780
You can call me Sonoko!

00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:25.300
She's just as bad…

00:30:25.300 --> 00:30:28.410
If Inspector Megure's division is here, then…

00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:33.310
That means the receptionist recognised the old man and thought he'd been called in to help in the investigation, so he brought us up here…

00:30:34.540 --> 00:30:35.850
Hey, did something happen?

00:30:35.850 --> 00:30:38.210
It's nothing to do with us.

00:30:39.750 --> 00:30:40.690
Inspector Megure,

00:30:42.690 --> 00:30:44.970
‘Takagi-was-fine.’

00:30:44.970 --> 00:30:47.470
‘But-the-Cherry-Sapphire-was—’…

00:30:47.470 --> 00:30:48.700
Lupin?!

00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:00.900
Lupin!

00:31:00.900 --> 00:31:02.960
Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

00:31:02.960 --> 00:31:05.050
Hi! I was worried about you!

00:31:05.050 --> 00:31:06.780
They didn't do anything bad to you?

00:31:06.780 --> 00:31:07.780
No.

00:31:07.780 --> 00:31:09.530
But I was so scared…

00:31:09.530 --> 00:31:14.050
Aww, they made you wear such an ugly necklace?

00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:17.720
You've got no fashion sense, you know.

00:31:18.580 --> 00:31:20.500
Let's get this done with.

00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:22.150
Hand it to Fujiko-<i>kun</i>.

00:31:22.150 --> 00:31:25.360
Hasty, aren't we? Don't like talking, then?

00:31:26.400 --> 00:31:27.930
That's enough!

00:31:27.930 --> 00:31:29.640
I'm not about to pull out a gun!

00:31:29.640 --> 00:31:32.320
Think about the situation I'm in! Honestly…

00:31:32.320 --> 00:31:36.240
Leave the box. Just take the Cherry Sapphire from inside.

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:38.480
Geez, you're such a downer…

00:31:38.480 --> 00:31:41.360
It doesn't look like he trapped it anyway.

00:31:41.940 --> 00:31:42.650
Huh?!

00:31:42.650 --> 00:31:44.920
Sorry about this!

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:47.090
So you really <i>were</i> working together…

00:31:47.090 --> 00:31:49.740
It's well-made, isn't it?

00:31:49.740 --> 00:31:51.740
But it's a fake.

00:31:51.740 --> 00:31:53.050
Oh, and…

00:31:54.950 --> 00:31:58.040
Sorry, but I'm not about to let you have it either.

00:31:58.040 --> 00:31:59.310
That's fine, right?

00:31:59.310 --> 00:32:00.920
Drop your weapons!

00:32:00.920 --> 00:32:03.690
Wow! Now that's the real Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

00:32:03.690 --> 00:32:08.780
…is what I'd like to say, but it looks like you were a bit naïve this time.

00:32:08.780 --> 00:32:10.490
Huh? What do you mean?

00:32:10.970 --> 00:32:14.110
That bomb's the real deal.

00:32:14.110 --> 00:32:15.850
No way!

00:32:16.560 --> 00:32:19.740
Deceiving an innocent little girl, you're the worst!

00:32:19.740 --> 00:32:22.020
If you want it so much, then take it!

00:32:23.020 --> 00:32:25.280
So? What happens now?

00:32:25.280 --> 00:32:29.630
You want to watch my head and body go their separate ways?

00:32:29.630 --> 00:32:33.450
It looks like you've mistaken my interests.

00:32:33.450 --> 00:32:35.890
The deal has been accomplished.

00:32:35.890 --> 00:32:40.290
As soon as we get to a safe place, I'll release the necklace.

00:32:40.290 --> 00:32:42.580
But if I were to find this is a fake…

00:32:42.580 --> 00:32:44.000
Don't worry about that!

00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:45.150
It's the real thing.

00:32:45.150 --> 00:32:46.840
Or what?

00:32:46.840 --> 00:32:49.570
You plan to say this was ‘just a test’ too?

00:32:49.570 --> 00:32:51.010
No.

00:32:51.010 --> 00:32:52.990
This is the end.

00:32:52.990 --> 00:32:55.430
You can have the car over there.

00:32:55.430 --> 00:32:57.850
As well as the coat inside it.

00:32:57.850 --> 00:32:58.990
Thanks a lot.

00:32:58.990 --> 00:33:03.520
I doubt we will ever meet again.

00:33:10.050 --> 00:33:15.620
This is her promoter for the Japanese concert, Luciano Carnevale-<i>san</i>.

00:33:15.620 --> 00:33:16.660
Hello.

00:33:16.660 --> 00:33:18.500
And this is…

00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:20.120
I'm Claudia Bellucci.

00:33:20.870 --> 00:33:23.310
Emilio's manager.

00:33:23.310 --> 00:33:25.250
Do I know that!

00:33:25.250 --> 00:33:27.090
We're here because—

00:33:27.090 --> 00:33:27.940
Inspector.

00:33:27.940 --> 00:33:30.230
Is it really okay to tell him?

00:33:30.230 --> 00:33:33.360
Despite appearances, you can trust Mouri-<i>san</i>.

00:33:33.930 --> 00:33:37.610
You didn't have to say ‘despite appearances’, but I hope I can be of help to you.

00:33:40.180 --> 00:33:41.030
The truth is…

00:33:41.560 --> 00:33:44.810
This morning, Emilio received this.

00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:47.500
This is…

00:33:54.950 --> 00:33:56.490
This is…!

00:34:01.140 --> 00:34:02.540
This is…

00:34:02.540 --> 00:34:03.770
…saying what exactly?

00:34:03.770 --> 00:34:07.960
You looked like you were on a roll, but you can't read it, huh?

00:34:09.520 --> 00:34:11.650
That's just like him…

00:34:15.780 --> 00:34:18.260
Newspaper clippings…

00:34:18.260 --> 00:34:19.280
Is that Italian?

00:34:19.640 --> 00:34:25.770
‘Cancel the live show, or Emilio dies.’

00:34:25.770 --> 00:34:27.160
No way!

00:34:27.160 --> 00:34:29.040
A threat?!

00:34:29.040 --> 00:34:32.430
He'll die, huh?

00:34:32.430 --> 00:34:34.920
Who here has touched this?

00:34:34.920 --> 00:34:37.120
I haven't touched it.

00:34:37.120 --> 00:34:39.430
Emilio and I have touched it.

00:34:39.430 --> 00:34:44.870
So if any fingerprints other than yours turn up, they'll be the culprit's…

00:34:44.870 --> 00:34:49.270
It sure would help if the senders of
threats left their fingerprints on them.

00:34:50.460 --> 00:34:52.020
Let's cancel it.

00:34:52.020 --> 00:34:53.550
I can't do this!

00:34:53.550 --> 00:34:55.220
All we have to do is cancel the concert, right?

00:34:55.220 --> 00:34:57.010
Calm down, Emilio.

00:34:57.010 --> 00:34:59.150
Cancelling it isn't as easy as you make it sound.

00:34:59.150 --> 00:35:03.770
We've already spent a fortune
 preparing for your Japanese concert.

00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:07.270
We even expedited the redevelopment of Tohto Stadium.

00:35:07.270 --> 00:35:10.170
The tickets are already sold out too.

00:35:10.170 --> 00:35:14.610
You know we can't just cancel it now, don't you?

00:35:16.490 --> 00:35:18.950
I'm begging you, Lupin.

00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:22.160
If you don't, this is gonna go ‘boom’!

00:35:22.160 --> 00:35:25.390
If you love me, then can you do this one job for me?

00:35:25.390 --> 00:35:27.830
Don't tease me.

00:35:27.830 --> 00:35:29.480
I'm suffering the consequences of that already.

00:35:29.480 --> 00:35:33.150
No, what I'm gonna tell you off about is the next bit.

00:35:33.550 --> 00:35:34.800
Never mind!

00:35:34.800 --> 00:35:36.690
I'll just ask Kid-<i>sama</i>!

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:38.800
Well, you know…

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:42.010
Do you get it now?

00:35:42.010 --> 00:35:42.950
What?

00:35:42.950 --> 00:35:46.990
There's only one man in the world who can protect you, Fujiko-<i>chan</i>.

00:35:46.990 --> 00:35:49.020
And who's that?!

00:35:49.020 --> 00:35:50.480
Lupin…

00:35:50.480 --> 00:35:53.500
Yeah! Time for reclining!

00:35:53.500 --> 00:35:54.990
No!

00:35:54.990 --> 00:35:55.990
Why?

00:35:55.990 --> 00:35:58.030
Hurry up and run…

00:35:58.030 --> 00:35:59.340
If you don't…

00:35:59.820 --> 00:36:04.340
Going out with you would my ideal way to go.

00:36:11.710 --> 00:36:13.590
That bastard!

00:36:13.590 --> 00:36:17.760
I'm gonna make him regret ever thinking about crossing me!

00:36:22.930 --> 00:36:26.240
Fujiko-<i>chan</i>, gimme back my clothes…

00:36:29.060 --> 00:36:31.250
Was it really okay to disarm it?

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:38.220
If we killed that woman, Lupin would come after us.

00:36:38.220 --> 00:36:39.880
We can't afford that now.

00:36:40.400 --> 00:36:44.840
For our homeland, we have to get <i>it</i>…

00:36:44.840 --> 00:36:50.330
It wasn't publicly announced that Emilio-<i>san</i> was staying in this hotel.

00:36:50.330 --> 00:36:54.960
The only people that knew were the concert staff, and some of the hotel employees.

00:36:54.960 --> 00:36:57.860
But we can't say for sure this wasn't an external threat.

00:36:57.860 --> 00:37:03.260
Crazed fans may go to extremes to find out where he is staying.

00:37:04.360 --> 00:37:09.020
We think it was probably just a prank, but
we'll post plain-clothes police officers nearby.

00:37:09.020 --> 00:37:10.160
That should help comfort y—

00:37:10.160 --> 00:37:11.810
I have identified the culprit!

00:37:13.020 --> 00:37:14.980
Really, Mouri-<i>kun</i>?

00:37:14.980 --> 00:37:16.020
Yes!

00:37:16.020 --> 00:37:18.380
The one who sent that threat was…

00:37:19.150 --> 00:37:20.750
Lupin III!

00:37:20.750 --> 00:37:21.950
Lupin?

00:37:21.950 --> 00:37:22.760
Lupin?!

00:37:22.760 --> 00:37:25.010
Seriously, old man?!

00:37:25.010 --> 00:37:29.370
He's a petty thief that's been causing
trouble in this city for the last two days.

00:37:29.370 --> 00:37:33.170
He shows off by stealing jewels, then throwing them away.

00:37:33.170 --> 00:37:35.520
He probably decides he doesn't want them.

00:37:35.880 --> 00:37:43.400
Wasn't your phone call earlier a report that Lupin's stolen another jewel, Shiratori?

00:37:43.400 --> 00:37:45.180
What happened, old man?!

00:37:45.180 --> 00:37:46.400
{Your mind's sharp for once!}You're actually being competent!

00:37:46.400 --> 00:37:52.240
We did just receive that report, but how does that connect with this threat?

00:37:52.240 --> 00:37:58.530
Forcing the concert to be cancelled, and looking for valuable jewels, there's only one thing Lupin could be after…

00:37:58.530 --> 00:37:59.990
And that is…

00:37:59.990 --> 00:38:01.250
It is…?

00:38:01.810 --> 00:38:03.070
Claudia-<i>san</i>!

00:38:03.760 --> 00:38:08.790
Just when you're depressed about the concert, he'll turn up and present you with a jewel.

00:38:08.790 --> 00:38:09.800
A present?

00:38:09.800 --> 00:38:11.200
Yes!

00:38:11.200 --> 00:38:13.680
He must be trying to seduce you!

00:38:13.680 --> 00:38:15.330
It's too dangerous here.

00:38:15.330 --> 00:38:17.670
You should stay at my house.

00:38:20.630 --> 00:38:21.560
Emilio!

00:38:22.550 --> 00:38:24.050
Don't worry.

00:38:24.050 --> 00:38:25.570
I'll stay in my room.

00:38:26.890 --> 00:38:28.970
But I didn't get his autograph yet…

00:38:28.970 --> 00:38:30.560
Let's go, Sonoko.

00:38:30.560 --> 00:38:32.310
It's not a good time.

00:38:33.240 --> 00:38:34.560
Conan-<i>kun</i>, let's go.

00:38:35.450 --> 00:38:36.370
Right!

00:38:38.730 --> 00:38:39.900
What about Uncle?

00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:42.110
No point trying to talk sense into him.

00:38:42.110 --> 00:38:42.630
Ain't that right.

00:38:43.030 --> 00:38:45.740
Anyway, we'll post guards around this floor of the hotel.

00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:47.780
You shouldn't have to.

00:38:47.780 --> 00:38:50.740
He's got a very reliable bodyguard, right?

00:38:50.740 --> 00:38:51.430
Huh?

00:38:51.430 --> 00:38:54.010
You sure are attentive, little boy.

00:38:54.010 --> 00:38:56.080
I saw him on TV!

00:38:56.080 --> 00:38:57.580
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:38:57.580 --> 00:38:59.040
Coming!

00:38:59.040 --> 00:39:01.400
You have a bodyguard you can rely on?

00:39:01.400 --> 00:39:07.550
He's a charismatic teacher, said to have tripled the military strength of one country just by teaching their soldiers.

00:39:07.550 --> 00:39:09.490
Wow, Daddy's amazing.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.810
We'll be leaving now.

00:39:13.020 --> 00:39:15.770
Hey, there was a sweet shop downstairs, wasn't there?

00:39:15.770 --> 00:39:17.080
Right, there was.

00:39:17.080 --> 00:39:18.730
You have sharp eyes.{sasuga mezatoi!}

00:39:18.730 --> 00:39:19.730
Let's go get some sweets.

00:39:19.730 --> 00:39:20.920
Yeah.

00:39:28.800 --> 00:39:31.280
One floor above the lobby, right?

00:39:31.280 --> 00:39:31.800
Yeah.

00:39:32.620 --> 00:39:34.580
Huh? Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:39:34.580 --> 00:39:35.100
Huh?

00:39:35.730 --> 00:39:38.430
Hey! We'll leave you behind, brat!

00:39:38.430 --> 00:39:40.080
Don't leave me behind!

00:39:45.420 --> 00:39:47.530
Now, let's go and have some fun.

00:39:48.470 --> 00:39:50.220
Huh? W-Wha…? B-But…

00:39:50.220 --> 00:39:53.220
That little brat's sure grown up!

00:39:53.220 --> 00:39:55.030
No, Sonoko, that's not it at all!

00:39:55.030 --> 00:39:56.940
So miracles do happen!

00:39:56.940 --> 00:39:58.790
Sonoko!

00:40:09.660 --> 00:40:11.630
Hey, wait…!

00:40:11.630 --> 00:40:19.020
Right now, I'm running with
 my shoulder being held by Emilio!

00:40:20.290 --> 00:40:22.270
Wait! Please, wait!

00:40:22.270 --> 00:40:24.770
Come on, stop!

00:40:27.800 --> 00:40:28.270
Sorry!

00:40:31.010 --> 00:40:33.260
Please, Sonoko, just think about this!

00:40:33.260 --> 00:40:35.680
Aren't you going to ask if I'm okay?

00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:36.720
We have to go back!

00:40:36.720 --> 00:40:38.850
He can't be out of his room now!

00:40:38.850 --> 00:40:39.440
Why not?

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:40.730
Why not?!

00:40:40.730 --> 00:40:42.360
He was threatened!

00:40:42.360 --> 00:40:44.520
What would we do if something happened to Emilio?!

00:40:44.520 --> 00:40:46.780
That's obviously just a prank!

00:40:46.780 --> 00:40:48.190
And that's for <i>you</i> to decide?

00:40:48.190 --> 00:40:50.700
It said that he'd die!

00:40:50.700 --> 00:40:51.910
Well, I didn't see that!

00:40:51.910 --> 00:40:53.170
Don't mess about!

00:40:53.660 --> 00:40:57.410
{Sonoko: I know everything'll be fine. You wanna know why?  Ran: Huh? Why?  Sonoko: You've broken knives with your kicks, dodged bullets at close-range, defended an Aegis Destroyer from a foreign spy, and even survived being thrown to the depths of the ocean. You're a supergirl!  Emilio: Wow, you did all that?  Ran: Huh? Well, it's not that much…  Sonoko: And }You even defeated the strongest bodyguard in all of Vespania!

00:40:57.410 --> 00:40:58.830
{Stop exaggerating!}Don't exaggerate!

00:40:58.830 --> 00:41:01.790
Anyway, there's nobody that can beat her within 10 kilometres!

00:41:01.790 --> 00:41:03.310
Sonoko…

00:41:03.710 --> 00:41:05.170
There!

00:41:05.170 --> 00:41:06.400
Let's go there!

00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:09.300
Sure! I'll go anywhere with you!

00:41:09.960 --> 00:41:13.640
They're gonna be mad at us!

00:41:33.740 --> 00:41:36.130
You want to dirty your nice clean lungs?

00:41:36.130 --> 00:41:40.790
This is the only place in the hotel
where you can smoke and drink alcohol.

00:41:41.660 --> 00:41:43.710
Hey, Great Detective.

00:41:43.710 --> 00:41:45.130
Excuse me, you shouldn't be here…

00:41:45.130 --> 00:41:48.130
Oh, I just came to see Daddy!

00:41:48.130 --> 00:41:50.590
Oh, is that so? Then can I get you some juice?

00:41:50.590 --> 00:41:52.130
He'll have an iced coffee.

00:41:53.090 --> 00:41:54.010
Coming straight up.

00:41:57.760 --> 00:41:59.470
What?

00:41:59.470 --> 00:42:03.290
You're not the only guy to drink
 iced coffee all year round, right?

00:42:04.230 --> 00:42:06.660
What are you planning here?

00:42:07.690 --> 00:42:09.670
So you're here as Shin'ichi Kudō, huh?

00:42:10.690 --> 00:42:12.570
Sorry for the wait.

00:42:12.570 --> 00:42:15.570
If you would like, feel free to try some lemon pie too.

00:42:15.570 --> 00:42:17.620
Wow! Thanks!

00:42:19.410 --> 00:42:21.430
Looks like you have it tough too.

00:42:21.990 --> 00:42:23.310
You idiot…

00:42:23.310 --> 00:42:25.830
Catchphrase: ‘You idiot’.

00:42:25.830 --> 00:42:27.670
Oh, and ‘I've gotta go to the toilet!’

00:42:27.670 --> 00:42:30.000
What are those notes?!

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.260
Bladder issues at your age?

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:33.470
You should see a doctor!

00:42:33.470 --> 00:42:34.690
You know that's not it!

00:42:35.370 --> 00:42:37.100
Now do you get it?

00:42:37.100 --> 00:42:39.240
Adults can be scary.

00:42:39.630 --> 00:42:41.810
So you're threatening me…

00:42:41.810 --> 00:42:43.890
Well, don't worry about it.

00:42:43.890 --> 00:42:47.870
If you don't stick your nose where it
doesn't belong, everything'll be peachy.

00:42:47.870 --> 00:42:51.750
Oh, didn't your notes say?

00:42:51.750 --> 00:42:55.130
I'm the sort of guy that just gets fired up when threatened.

00:42:56.660 --> 00:42:58.870
Agh, what a pain!

00:42:58.870 --> 00:43:00.080
I'll have some pie!

00:43:00.080 --> 00:43:02.450
Oh! You called me ‘Daddy’, didn't you?!

00:43:02.450 --> 00:43:03.450
You're worried about that <i>now</i>?!

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:07.210
It's me.

00:43:07.210 --> 00:43:08.770
What is it, Ran-<i>neechan</i>?

00:43:08.770 --> 00:43:10.170
Emilio's gone?!

00:43:10.170 --> 00:43:11.270
You're with Emilio?!

00:43:11.270 --> 00:43:13.270
What do you mean, you're not with him?

00:43:13.270 --> 00:43:15.020
Sonoko's here too.

00:43:15.020 --> 00:43:16.730
Everyone's looking for him.

00:43:16.730 --> 00:43:20.010
He just wants to go up before coming back, so tell Dad and the others—

00:43:20.010 --> 00:43:21.680
Okay, I'll be taking this!

00:43:21.680 --> 00:43:23.320
No, give it back!

00:43:23.320 --> 00:43:25.180
Wait—

00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:28.830
Sounds like someone's having fun…

00:43:28.830 --> 00:43:30.400
Right.

00:43:30.400 --> 00:43:31.820
Got it.

00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:36.570
What was your call about?

00:43:36.570 --> 00:43:37.990
Yummy!

00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:42.120
Sounds like they're with Emilio.

00:43:42.120 --> 00:43:43.330
Guess so.

00:43:43.330 --> 00:43:44.750
Where are they?

00:43:44.750 --> 00:43:46.290
No idea.

00:43:46.290 --> 00:43:49.000
Let's be grown-ups here.

00:43:49.000 --> 00:43:50.330
I'm leaving.

00:43:51.210 --> 00:43:54.880
Okay, okay! I'll screw up these notes!

00:43:54.880 --> 00:43:55.550
Look!

00:43:55.550 --> 00:43:57.590
I'll throw them out, okay!

00:43:59.010 --> 00:44:00.820
Daddy's sorry…

00:44:04.820 --> 00:44:06.350
It's so fast!

00:44:06.350 --> 00:44:08.020
It's amazing.

00:44:08.020 --> 00:44:09.950
Is this really okay?

00:44:09.950 --> 00:44:12.400
What's that bodyguard doing?

00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:14.190
Talking won't find him.

00:44:14.190 --> 00:44:16.210
We should look around here for him too.

00:44:16.210 --> 00:44:18.400
The police are gone, right?

00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:21.120
Yes, though that detective's still around.

00:44:21.120 --> 00:44:22.580
He went to look for him?

00:44:22.580 --> 00:44:23.370
Yes.

00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:26.370
What a useless bodyguard!

00:44:30.790 --> 00:44:32.230
Well, sorry about that.

00:44:32.230 --> 00:44:35.980
I'll be saying farewell when I'm done anyway…

00:44:45.990 --> 00:44:48.480
If it's anywhere, it'll be here…

00:44:52.610 --> 00:44:55.170
What a pretty sunset!

00:44:55.170 --> 00:44:57.360
He's pretty too!

00:44:59.490 --> 00:45:02.370
Ran, you'll scare people…

00:45:02.370 --> 00:45:05.180
It's no good… Everyone looks suspicious…

00:45:05.620 --> 00:45:08.700
Hey, let's head back…!

00:45:11.790 --> 00:45:13.460
It couldn't be…

00:45:14.590 --> 00:45:16.550
Guess I should check in here too…

00:45:27.640 --> 00:45:30.020
He even changed his shoes…

00:45:43.270 --> 00:45:44.170
It's me.

00:45:44.170 --> 00:45:46.950
You were right. It's not in the hotel.

00:45:47.660 --> 00:45:50.200
Yeah. The concert equipment, you think?

00:45:52.330 --> 00:45:53.420
What?

00:45:53.420 --> 00:45:54.680
Don't ‘what’ me.

00:45:56.420 --> 00:45:59.300
You said you were going on ahead to the tower, didn't you?

00:45:59.300 --> 00:46:01.510
I thought I'd go there with you, Daddy.

00:46:01.510 --> 00:46:02.840
Liar.

00:46:02.840 --> 00:46:05.610
Should a bodyguard really have a spare key?

00:46:07.050 --> 00:46:10.350
You gonna turn me in even though I haven't stolen anything?

00:46:10.350 --> 00:46:13.020
Possession of a gun is reason enough, right?

00:46:13.020 --> 00:46:17.150
Lemme tell you something, father to son.

00:46:17.150 --> 00:46:21.990
The plan this time has nothing to do with your lot, so how about leaving us alone?

00:46:24.160 --> 00:46:25.780
What do you say?

00:46:25.780 --> 00:46:26.590
No way.

00:46:29.590 --> 00:46:31.580
Hey, Miss…

00:46:31.580 --> 00:46:33.370
Hi! What is it, little guy?

00:46:33.370 --> 00:46:35.540
Do you have any newspapers in Italian?

00:46:35.540 --> 00:46:39.600
Sorry, we only have English newspapers here in the hotel.

00:46:39.600 --> 00:46:40.880
Are you looking for one?

00:46:40.880 --> 00:46:42.470
Nah, I'll be fine.

00:46:42.470 --> 00:46:44.180
Thanks!

00:46:49.100 --> 00:46:50.890
Uh, can I ask you something?

00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:51.990
What is it, my darling?

00:46:51.990 --> 00:46:54.640
I'd like to go in there…

00:46:54.640 --> 00:46:57.000
Ah, er, go ahead…

00:47:00.360 --> 00:47:02.340
Hi. You took your time.

00:47:02.340 --> 00:47:04.840
Huh? What do you mean?

00:47:04.840 --> 00:47:06.160
{Haibara: Lupin stole another jewel.}Yeah.

00:47:06.860 --> 00:47:08.970
I knew about the Lupin trouble.

00:47:08.970 --> 00:47:11.700
What he stole was the Cherry Sapphire.

00:47:11.700 --> 00:47:14.600
It was in the Tohto Bank vault.

00:47:14.910 --> 00:47:17.170
Is there something special about that jewel?

00:47:18.080 --> 00:47:21.210
It's not special at all.

00:47:21.210 --> 00:47:22.860
I can't even find anything about it.

00:47:22.860 --> 00:47:25.630
But Lupin even issued a theft notice…

00:47:26.470 --> 00:47:29.200
That's it! The jewel's owner!

00:47:29.200 --> 00:47:31.140
Ding-dong!

00:47:31.140 --> 00:47:33.620
You finally caught up with Kojima-<i>kun</i> and the others.

00:47:33.620 --> 00:47:37.290
Caught up? Oh, don't tell me they're at it again!

00:47:37.650 --> 00:47:39.440
They're all fired up.

00:47:39.440 --> 00:47:41.290
Even more than usual.

00:47:41.940 --> 00:47:46.920
They've been investigating vacant houses all over town
since morning, even checking their lawns and basements.

00:47:46.920 --> 00:47:49.410
Searching for Lupin's hideout?

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:51.430
We wouldn't need police if it could be found that easily…

00:47:51.430 --> 00:47:52.870
They found it.

00:47:52.870 --> 00:47:53.790
No way!

00:47:53.790 --> 00:47:57.330
The Cherry Sapphire's owner is Eishin Wakagomo.

00:47:57.330 --> 00:48:03.090
Would someone who uses a safe-deposit box
at a bank really live at a bankrupt mechanic's?

00:48:03.090 --> 00:48:05.880
And the shutters over the entrance

00:48:05.880 --> 00:48:07.320
have recently been refurbished.

00:48:07.320 --> 00:48:09.940
They've found out that much?!

00:48:10.510 --> 00:48:12.320
The doctor's enthusiastically helping them too.

00:48:12.320 --> 00:48:14.390
Oh, Doc…

00:48:14.390 --> 00:48:16.330
I can't stop them by myself, you know.

00:48:16.770 --> 00:48:18.190
It's too dangerous!

00:48:18.190 --> 00:48:19.700
Don't let them go anywhere until I get back!

00:48:19.700 --> 00:48:22.210
Honestly…!

00:48:22.210 --> 00:48:25.440
Let's catch Lupin, and go to Hawaii!

00:48:25.440 --> 00:48:27.070
Yeah!

00:48:27.070 --> 00:48:28.280
This is hopeless.

00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:31.090
What is it?

00:48:31.090 --> 00:48:33.240
I forgot why I was calling.

00:48:33.240 --> 00:48:35.430
Emilio's manager and promoter!

00:48:37.580 --> 00:48:39.000
Okay.

00:48:39.000 --> 00:48:40.930
Got it. I'll look into them.

00:48:40.930 --> 00:48:43.290
So what are you do—

00:48:45.340 --> 00:48:46.730
How selfish…

00:48:47.370 --> 00:48:48.760
Was he there?

00:48:48.760 --> 00:48:49.550
No luck.

00:48:49.550 --> 00:48:51.510
Maybe he went down without us?

00:48:51.510 --> 00:48:53.240
He must've just pretended to go in there…

00:48:53.240 --> 00:48:55.720
We haven't taken our eyes off the men's since…

00:48:55.720 --> 00:48:57.770
He must've planned to get away from us.

00:48:57.770 --> 00:48:58.490
Why?

00:48:58.490 --> 00:48:59.890
I don't know…

00:48:59.890 --> 00:49:00.980
Anyway, we have to find him!

00:49:00.980 --> 00:49:01.730
Yeah.

00:49:05.780 --> 00:49:08.190
You're really sure it was Emilio?

00:49:08.190 --> 00:49:09.360
Huh?

00:49:09.360 --> 00:49:10.250
He's not even here.

00:49:10.250 --> 00:49:12.570
I'm telling you, he was!

00:49:12.570 --> 00:49:15.410
Why would Emilio be here alone?

00:49:15.410 --> 00:49:17.180
Have you seen Emilio?

00:49:17.180 --> 00:49:18.750
Miss, you are…?

00:49:18.750 --> 00:49:21.040
A-A staff member for his Japan tour.

00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:23.020
So it really <i>was</i> him!

00:49:23.730 --> 00:49:25.520
You look so cute!

00:49:25.520 --> 00:49:29.130
…he said, so I went to get a board for him to sign.

00:49:29.130 --> 00:49:30.440
You're supposed to be working…

00:49:31.260 --> 00:49:32.440
Miss?

00:49:33.940 --> 00:49:35.510
You can't go that way!

00:49:35.510 --> 00:49:36.890
Call the supervisor!

00:49:38.430 --> 00:49:40.370
You took long enough.

00:49:40.370 --> 00:49:41.980
Sorry, sorry…

00:49:41.980 --> 00:49:43.310
Time to buy tickets.

00:49:43.310 --> 00:49:44.650
Hmph. Here!

00:49:44.650 --> 00:49:46.730
Wow! You're so kind!

00:49:46.730 --> 00:49:47.880
Don't make fun of me!

00:50:09.260 --> 00:50:11.800
What are you doing, Emilio?!

00:50:12.550 --> 00:50:13.650
Ran-<i>san</i>!

00:50:13.650 --> 00:50:17.180
You shouldn't have come up here.

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:18.560
Don't mess around.

00:50:18.560 --> 00:50:19.560
Don't come any closer!

00:50:21.930 --> 00:50:24.150
Please tell me…

00:50:24.150 --> 00:50:25.500
Why are you doing this?

00:50:25.870 --> 00:50:27.630
It's the concert…

00:50:27.630 --> 00:50:29.020
I can't do it…

00:50:31.150 --> 00:50:34.430
Is that it? You must be overworked.

00:50:34.430 --> 00:50:36.760
I agree, maybe you should take a break—

00:50:36.760 --> 00:50:38.160
No!

00:50:38.160 --> 00:50:41.600
As long as I'm still around, they won't cancel the concert.

00:50:43.330 --> 00:50:44.600
N-No way…

00:50:44.600 --> 00:50:46.380
That's not right!

00:50:46.380 --> 00:50:50.230
There's no way a concert can be
more important than someone's life!

00:50:50.230 --> 00:50:53.840
If they won't cancel it, then I…

00:50:53.840 --> 00:50:55.220
I—

00:50:57.090 --> 00:51:00.530
Anyway, please, just come back over here!

00:51:01.930 --> 00:51:03.680
We're the only ones here.

00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:06.540
Because we're going up so late.

00:51:06.540 --> 00:51:10.070
But they are up here, right?

00:51:10.070 --> 00:51:12.170
I haven't heard that they've come back yet.

00:51:12.740 --> 00:51:16.050
Hey, do you have a hideout in this town too, Daddy?

00:51:16.050 --> 00:51:20.780
You know, don't start thinking I'll tell you everything just cause you sound like a kid.

00:51:20.780 --> 00:51:22.240
So you do!

00:51:22.240 --> 00:51:23.800
How'd I get into this?!

00:51:24.370 --> 00:51:26.410
No…

00:51:26.410 --> 00:51:28.520
You can't…

00:51:29.160 --> 00:51:31.590
I'm begging you…

00:51:31.590 --> 00:51:35.400
Just please, let's talk this through!

00:51:37.760 --> 00:51:39.400
I…

00:51:42.560 --> 00:51:44.480
Emilio…

00:51:55.610 --> 00:51:57.250
Grab my arm!

00:52:03.260 --> 00:52:05.160
Ran-<i>san</i>!

00:52:05.160 --> 00:52:05.760
I can't…

00:52:06.400 --> 00:52:08.420
You'll be fine!

00:52:08.420 --> 00:52:10.390
Can you reach your feet into that gap?

00:52:11.920 --> 00:52:12.980
Sure!

00:52:25.820 --> 00:52:26.870
Ran!

00:52:26.870 --> 00:52:28.490
Sonoko!

00:52:28.490 --> 00:52:30.290
I don't wanna hear you whimpering!

00:52:30.850 --> 00:52:33.960
Ran Mouri's the greatest girl there ever was!

00:52:33.960 --> 00:52:35.710
I'll pull you both up!

00:52:35.710 --> 00:52:37.460
One, two…!

00:52:43.410 --> 00:52:44.590
No!

00:52:59.840 --> 00:53:01.220
Sonoko!

00:53:01.780 --> 00:53:03.070
Ra—

00:53:04.740 --> 00:53:06.020
Hey, old man!

00:53:06.020 --> 00:53:06.870
Can you break through this?

00:53:06.870 --> 00:53:09.000
Is it that girl hanging down there?

00:53:09.000 --> 00:53:09.620
Yeah.

00:53:09.620 --> 00:53:10.560
Thickness?

00:53:10.560 --> 00:53:11.480
2 panes, 10mm.

00:53:11.480 --> 00:53:12.440
Size of the hole?

00:53:12.440 --> 00:53:13.210
So I can jump!

00:53:13.210 --> 00:53:14.960
Twelve shots then!

00:53:25.030 --> 00:53:26.160
Ran!

00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:28.350
Don't you dare let go of Emilio!

00:53:28.790 --> 00:53:30.660
I'm gonna give him a big slap!

00:53:30.660 --> 00:53:33.250
Doing this to my best friend…

00:53:33.250 --> 00:53:34.350
What sort of monster are you?!

00:53:34.750 --> 00:53:38.360
I wanna slap you so hard you turn ugly!

00:53:38.360 --> 00:53:40.860
S-Sonoko…

00:53:41.650 --> 00:53:43.150
Can you do it?

00:53:45.600 --> 00:53:47.890
I'm sorry… Sonoko…

00:53:48.930 --> 00:53:53.410
I can't hold on…

00:53:53.410 --> 00:53:55.440
Ran!

00:53:55.440 --> 00:53:56.610
Ran!

00:53:57.290 --> 00:53:58.530
Ran!

00:53:58.530 --> 00:54:01.320
Ran-<i>neechan</i>!

00:54:03.050 --> 00:54:04.300
The brat?!

00:54:04.300 --> 00:54:05.630
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:54:19.440 --> 00:54:21.670
Thank you, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:54:22.320 --> 00:54:25.090
Brilliant! Brilliant, brat!

00:54:25.090 --> 00:54:27.320
I'll give you a big hug later!

00:54:27.320 --> 00:54:29.820
You don't have to go that far…

00:54:30.470 --> 00:54:33.040
E-Excuse me, what are you doing?

00:54:33.040 --> 00:54:34.790
What am I doing?

00:54:36.020 --> 00:54:38.790
Saving lives.

00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:42.000
Like I said, everything's fine. Don't worry.

00:54:45.880 --> 00:54:47.660
You…

00:54:47.660 --> 00:54:53.390
You didn't just put yourself in danger, but other people too!

00:54:53.960 --> 00:54:56.730
Do you understand the severity of what you did?

00:54:57.130 --> 00:54:59.040
Just think about it!

00:55:02.380 --> 00:55:05.970
Will you help us?

00:55:07.590 --> 00:55:08.990
Don't worry.

00:55:08.990 --> 00:55:11.370
The concert's not being cancelled.

00:55:11.370 --> 00:55:13.970
I would hope not.

00:55:13.970 --> 00:55:19.000
But don't you think your star has a bit too much freedom?

00:55:19.000 --> 00:55:23.840
If he causes too many problems,
 it might affect our deal, capisce?

00:55:23.840 --> 00:55:27.200
Is that why you called?

00:55:27.200 --> 00:55:30.090
Doing anything now will just be a bigger risk.

00:55:30.510 --> 00:55:31.740
Yes…

00:55:31.740 --> 00:55:34.300
The time and place will be as we agreed.

00:55:35.500 --> 00:55:38.060
Does Claudia-<i>san</i> know too?

00:55:38.060 --> 00:55:39.460
She does.

00:55:40.090 --> 00:55:43.860
Or rather, she's known all along, and is even helping.

00:55:43.860 --> 00:55:47.780
What exactly is this black-market deal?

00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:49.670
I don't know…

00:55:49.670 --> 00:55:55.660
When we're on stage during the main act of the concert, that must be when they do it…

00:55:55.660 --> 00:55:59.660
They started when Luciano became your promoter?

00:55:59.660 --> 00:56:00.860
Yeah.

00:56:00.860 --> 00:56:02.690
He changed everything.

00:56:02.690 --> 00:56:03.710
The songs, the stages…

00:56:04.230 --> 00:56:06.320
He even got TV channels involved.

00:56:06.320 --> 00:56:08.570
And he didn't even listen to my demo tapes!

00:56:09.210 --> 00:56:13.220
But most important to me is Claudia.

00:56:13.220 --> 00:56:18.620
She's happier and loves my songs more than anyone else.

00:56:19.220 --> 00:56:23.730
So you thought that if the concert
was cancelled, the deals would stop?

00:56:23.730 --> 00:56:26.010
I'm so sorry…

00:56:26.010 --> 00:56:28.260
I didn't really intend to jump off.

00:56:28.260 --> 00:56:30.990
I guess I sorta misunderstood too…

00:56:31.400 --> 00:56:33.490
I'm sorry for hitting you.

00:56:33.490 --> 00:56:35.430
I understand.

00:56:35.430 --> 00:56:37.810
You really wanted to help me.

00:56:38.810 --> 00:56:40.310
Oh, sorry.

00:56:40.310 --> 00:56:41.500
I should give this back.

00:56:41.500 --> 00:56:43.600
Yeah.

00:56:43.600 --> 00:56:44.670
It's Dad!

00:56:44.670 --> 00:56:46.240
Yes?

00:56:46.240 --> 00:56:47.320
Yeah…

00:56:47.320 --> 00:56:49.000
I know…

00:56:49.000 --> 00:56:50.950
Actually, I'm with him now.

00:56:50.950 --> 00:56:54.200
You don't have to shout!

00:56:54.200 --> 00:56:56.250
What do you think of this paper clipping?

00:56:56.250 --> 00:56:56.720
Huh?

00:56:57.170 --> 00:56:59.220
It was in your room, Emilio.

00:56:59.220 --> 00:57:01.880
T-That was in my room?

00:57:01.880 --> 00:57:03.230
Don't try and hide it.

00:57:03.230 --> 00:57:11.430
That hotel doesn't have any Italian newspapers, and Claudia-<i>san</i> understood that threat without any trouble at all.

00:57:11.430 --> 00:57:15.990
Which means that this K didn't just fall off of it.

00:57:15.990 --> 00:57:17.930
Right.

00:57:17.930 --> 00:57:21.240
She'd have noticed if it had fallen off when it was opened.

00:57:21.240 --> 00:57:24.400
There were some faint marks on the table too.

00:57:24.400 --> 00:57:25.870
You used a box cutter, didn't you?

00:57:26.290 --> 00:57:30.250
There's no K in the Italian alphabet to begin with.

00:57:30.250 --> 00:57:32.640
Time to get rid of the evidence!

00:57:32.640 --> 00:57:33.670
Too little too late, huh?

00:57:33.670 --> 00:57:37.590
Glamorous hotels don't throw out guests' rubbish immediately.

00:57:37.590 --> 00:57:41.350
You'll have to hide the cutter and
the papers as soon as we get back.

00:57:41.350 --> 00:57:44.420
Not to mention the glue…

00:57:44.420 --> 00:57:46.850
The Japanese police are great, you know.

00:57:47.460 --> 00:57:49.720
With everything you did on the tower earlier…

00:57:49.720 --> 00:57:52.760
Just who are you?

00:57:52.760 --> 00:57:56.610
Conan Edogawa, detective.

00:57:56.610 --> 00:57:59.470
Is that a catchphrase?

00:57:59.470 --> 00:58:00.930
Or something he stole?

00:58:00.930 --> 00:58:03.370
I get the feeling you're an amazing boy…

00:58:03.370 --> 00:58:05.980
There's so many fans waiting for you.

00:58:05.980 --> 00:58:07.620
Give the concert all you've got.

00:58:09.130 --> 00:58:11.780
I won't let the deal happen.

00:58:11.780 --> 00:58:12.950
And…

00:58:12.950 --> 00:58:15.010
I'll catch all of the bad guys.

00:58:18.410 --> 00:58:20.500
We've been looking for you!

00:58:20.500 --> 00:58:23.810
You shouldn't be out here at a time like this.

00:58:24.560 --> 00:58:28.750
Do you honestly understand just how worried we were?

00:58:28.750 --> 00:58:31.440
Do you realise how much trouble you've caused?

00:58:32.800 --> 00:58:34.840
Thank you very much.

00:58:34.840 --> 00:58:37.950
I don't know what would've happened if you hadn't found him, Mouri-<i>san</i>.

00:58:37.950 --> 00:58:39.430
That's more than enough.

00:58:39.430 --> 00:58:41.950
Finding missing persons is the simplest job a detective has.

00:58:41.950 --> 00:58:46.650
Emilio, don't think that everyone will be so accepting of your selfish actions—

00:58:46.650 --> 00:58:47.960
I'm sorry.

00:58:47.960 --> 00:58:50.900
I've been getting carried away since we arrived in Japan.

00:58:50.900 --> 00:58:52.360
I regret it.

00:58:52.990 --> 00:58:55.160
Please forgive me, Claudia.

00:58:55.160 --> 00:58:58.410
I'll show you that this isn't an empty
apology by doing my best at the concert.

00:58:58.970 --> 00:59:01.870
Let's make it the greatest concert I've ever had!

00:59:01.870 --> 00:59:03.040
Luciano!

00:59:04.100 --> 00:59:06.540
I'll go and check in with the crew.


00:59:06.540 --> 00:59:08.520
The stage checks aren't until tomorrow.

00:59:08.520 --> 00:59:12.770
I was going to apologise to the
crew members I caused trouble for.

00:59:12.770 --> 00:59:14.650
O-Oh, right.

00:59:14.650 --> 00:59:15.900
That's a good idea.

00:59:20.640 --> 00:59:21.660
Mouri-<i>san</i>!

00:59:21.660 --> 00:59:24.890
What did you tell Emilio?!

00:59:29.150 --> 00:59:32.570
Just the common sense of what
it means to be an adult, I guess.

00:59:38.070 --> 00:59:39.470
It is I.

00:59:39.830 --> 00:59:47.100
You better abandon that hideout.
That brat's bratty pals may be coming for a visit.

00:59:47.100 --> 00:59:48.830
And if they were to…

00:59:48.830 --> 00:59:51.100
What would you have me do?

00:59:51.100 --> 00:59:53.510
They've all got their phones turned off.

00:59:53.510 --> 00:59:54.610
Are they with you?

00:59:54.610 --> 00:59:57.550
They all went to sleep early to be ready for tomorrow.

00:59:57.550 --> 00:59:59.490
Even the doctor's fast asleep.

00:59:59.490 --> 01:00:00.740
They couldn't have…

01:00:00.740 --> 01:00:02.030
They just could have.

01:00:02.030 --> 01:00:05.270
He's pointing straight at me…

01:00:06.230 --> 01:00:07.540
They couldn't have…

01:00:08.100 --> 01:00:09.830
They certainly have.

01:00:11.830 --> 01:00:14.900
We've always admired you!

01:00:14.900 --> 01:00:16.420
Welcome to Japan!

01:00:16.950 --> 01:00:19.010
I'm so impressed to meet you!

01:00:19.010 --> 01:00:21.010
‘Kitten Eggs’

01:00:19.010 --> 01:00:21.010
Please take this little gift.

01:00:21.010 --> 01:00:22.620
Go ahead!

01:00:22.620 --> 01:00:23.790
They're tasty!

01:00:23.790 --> 01:00:25.540
There's nothing weird inside either.

01:00:25.540 --> 01:00:26.460
Go on!

01:00:26.460 --> 01:00:28.060
I must express my gratitude.

01:00:28.060 --> 01:00:29.120
Got it?

01:00:29.120 --> 01:00:30.790
Just like we planned.

01:00:30.790 --> 01:00:32.210
When he's asleep…

01:00:32.210 --> 01:00:33.550
…we tie him up!

01:00:33.550 --> 01:00:35.170
With a reef knot, right?

01:00:35.170 --> 01:00:37.550
Then before long…

01:00:43.810 --> 01:00:45.950
May I offer you some tea?

01:00:52.310 --> 01:00:53.440
Are they asleep?

01:00:53.440 --> 01:00:55.130
Undoubtedly.

01:00:56.440 --> 01:00:59.880
Why'd I have to hide in the first place?

01:00:59.880 --> 01:01:02.530
Don't they know not to drink what they're given?

01:01:02.530 --> 01:01:04.890
And they call themselves detectives…

01:01:04.890 --> 01:01:07.540
Let's check out what they've got…

01:01:07.540 --> 01:01:08.890
You would strip a girl?

01:01:08.890 --> 01:01:11.210
Don't call it stripping!

01:01:14.630 --> 01:01:16.310
Ah! Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

01:01:16.830 --> 01:01:19.570
Unfortunately for you, looks like this is the end.

01:01:19.570 --> 01:01:23.140
Thanks to you lot, I got fired as a bodyguard.

01:01:23.140 --> 01:01:26.520
So I don't need to stick about any longer.

01:01:26.520 --> 01:01:27.430
See ya.

01:01:29.850 --> 01:01:33.270
How dare you kidnap my friends!

01:01:33.270 --> 01:01:36.360
Hmph! You've played that trick before.

01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:38.900
That's not gonna work again.

01:01:38.900 --> 01:01:40.150
I'm an adult, you know.

01:01:40.150 --> 01:01:42.720
Thief!

01:01:42.720 --> 01:01:44.870
You brat! How dare you shout that!

01:01:44.870 --> 01:01:46.120
Of course <i>that</i>'s gonna get me moving!

01:01:46.120 --> 01:01:47.080
Take a look at this.

01:01:47.080 --> 01:01:49.790
I just got some information about Luciano-<i>san</i>.

01:01:49.790 --> 01:01:50.680
You listening to me?!

01:01:51.080 --> 01:01:52.520
Italian Mafia?

01:01:52.830 --> 01:01:57.900
And according to HQ, he's planning a big deal right here in Japan.

01:01:57.900 --> 01:01:59.710
That's Lupin's goal?

01:01:59.710 --> 01:02:01.340
I guess so.

01:02:01.340 --> 01:02:04.820
Coming from you, that sounds pretty unsure, Inspector Zenigata.

01:02:04.820 --> 01:02:06.950
Is there something bothering you about it?

01:02:07.430 --> 01:02:09.310
It's too small a target…

01:02:09.310 --> 01:02:13.100
Does he want the jewel, or to stop the deal?

01:02:13.100 --> 01:02:15.460
It's not like him, you mean?

01:02:15.460 --> 01:02:18.170
He's not the type of guy Lupin would fight.

01:02:18.170 --> 01:02:20.990
H-He works on types, then?

01:02:20.990 --> 01:02:22.570
How did things go for you?

01:02:22.570 --> 01:02:24.110
I've finished my checks.

01:02:24.110 --> 01:02:26.050
But there's no point anymore.

01:02:26.050 --> 01:02:27.950
No point?

01:02:27.950 --> 01:02:30.660
Apparently he's not even going to file a damage report.

01:02:30.660 --> 01:02:32.310
This has been rather fishy to start with…

01:02:32.310 --> 01:02:37.190
Would someone involved in a backroom deal like
that really call the police in right before the deal?

01:02:37.190 --> 01:02:41.060
So there's someone among
 them who wants to interfere.

01:02:41.060 --> 01:02:43.320
Let's investigate.

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:45.820
What're all those toys?

01:02:45.820 --> 01:02:49.390
For some reason, they're all super gadgets.

01:02:49.390 --> 01:02:51.570
Not to mention masterfully designed.

01:02:51.570 --> 01:02:56.580
Whoever gives gadgets to brats
 like these ain't too great an adult.

01:02:56.580 --> 01:02:59.190
So what're you doing, Fujiko-<i>chan</i>?

01:02:59.190 --> 01:03:00.080
Fleeing into the night?

01:03:00.080 --> 01:03:01.320
You have to ask?

01:03:01.320 --> 01:03:02.960
I'm going to crush them.

01:03:02.960 --> 01:03:05.860
What a violent remark to come from those lips.

01:03:05.860 --> 01:03:07.720
It'll be dangerous all by yourself.

01:03:07.720 --> 01:03:09.630
Who said I was going alone?

01:03:09.630 --> 01:03:11.910
Don't tell me… Your friends again?

01:03:11.910 --> 01:03:13.040
I asked for their help.

01:03:13.040 --> 01:03:14.710
Which friends this time?

01:03:14.710 --> 01:03:15.670
All of them.

01:03:17.080 --> 01:03:19.020
Thus begins World War III.

01:03:19.020 --> 01:03:20.710
Relax!

01:03:20.710 --> 01:03:22.810
They won't get in your way.

01:03:22.810 --> 01:03:27.640
And I told them to only use ordinary weapons.

01:03:27.640 --> 01:03:29.470
That should reassure us?

01:03:29.470 --> 01:03:31.700
You mean you've found what we're doing?

01:03:31.700 --> 01:03:34.530
Like I said, we won't be in your way.

01:03:34.530 --> 01:03:36.600
Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

01:03:36.600 --> 01:03:38.230
Put those kids in the back.

01:03:38.230 --> 01:03:39.790
I'll take them back on my way.

01:03:39.790 --> 01:03:42.190
Huh? Where're you going?

01:03:42.190 --> 01:03:45.400
I'm not sticking around a hideout this filthy, that's for sure.

01:03:45.400 --> 01:03:47.320
I just came to pick up a few weapons.

01:03:47.990 --> 01:03:50.150
I'll tell you this much.

01:03:50.150 --> 01:03:52.790
We're gonna snatch it from both of them, like you deduced.

01:03:52.790 --> 01:03:54.330
At the concert?

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:55.370
Yeah…

01:03:55.370 --> 01:03:58.960
You tell the police and Zenigata, then pull out completely.

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:01.670
That's where a detective's job ends, right?

01:04:01.670 --> 01:04:03.270
That's your second warning.

01:04:03.270 --> 01:04:05.110
I won't give you a third.

01:04:05.980 --> 01:04:09.680
I told you I won't let the deal go through.

01:04:09.680 --> 01:04:11.110
I promised I won't let it happen!

01:04:13.390 --> 01:04:15.120
Tell Lupin that!

01:04:33.790 --> 01:04:35.260
Good evening.

01:04:35.260 --> 01:04:37.120
Fujiko Mine…

01:04:39.290 --> 01:04:41.180
What should I do with these kids?

01:04:41.180 --> 01:04:44.710
They might catch a cold out here.

01:04:44.710 --> 01:04:52.100
I'd like you to take them in, but can
you promise that you'll come with me?

01:05:03.820 --> 01:05:06.780
The Prince of Music, Emilio Barretti!

01:05:06.780 --> 01:05:08.240
It's not far now!

01:05:08.240 --> 01:05:11.070
Tomorrow is when we can hear him sing!

01:05:11.070 --> 01:05:12.280
Good, okay!

01:05:12.280 --> 01:05:15.340
Good, now let's interview the
fans who will be in line all night!

01:05:19.660 --> 01:05:23.230
To be doing black-market deals in a stadium full of people…

01:05:23.710 --> 01:05:25.210
I've been thinking about that.

01:05:25.210 --> 01:05:29.510
When the concert starts, everyone will be focused on the stage.

01:05:29.510 --> 01:05:33.530
Apparently Luciano was even involved with the stadium's remodelling.

01:05:33.850 --> 01:05:37.150
The backing band's dressing rooms and the basement underneath the stage…

01:05:37.640 --> 01:05:40.160
During the concert, they'll be empty.

01:05:40.160 --> 01:05:42.730
Any progress hacking the stadium cameras?

01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:44.290
Already done.

01:05:44.290 --> 01:05:47.630
Do you realise just how dangerous that was?!

01:05:47.630 --> 01:05:50.630
If it hadn't been sleeping pills
 in that tea, you'd all be long gone!

01:05:50.630 --> 01:05:53.490
Honestly, you had to leave me behind!

01:05:53.490 --> 01:05:55.120
Doc!

01:05:55.120 --> 01:05:56.630
Oh, sorry…

01:05:56.630 --> 01:05:59.410
I'll do something about Haibara myself.

01:05:59.410 --> 01:06:01.080
Right.

01:06:01.080 --> 01:06:02.470
You're all grounded!

01:06:02.470 --> 01:06:04.080
Right…

01:06:05.790 --> 01:06:07.710
Just as planned!

01:06:07.710 --> 01:06:09.510
He's not getting in our way!

01:06:09.510 --> 01:06:12.090
Haibara did great, going undercover for us!

01:06:12.090 --> 01:06:14.780
Conan-<i>kun</i>'ll be so shocked later!

01:06:15.140 --> 01:06:18.350
We move out as soon as we hear from Ai-<i>kun</i>.

01:06:18.350 --> 01:06:19.280
Yeah!

01:06:19.600 --> 01:06:20.640
Geez.

01:06:23.600 --> 01:06:24.520
Yes?

01:06:24.520 --> 01:06:26.040
Oh, I'm fine.

01:06:26.360 --> 01:06:28.610
For some reason, I'm being treated great.

01:06:29.230 --> 01:06:30.360
Yes…

01:06:30.360 --> 01:06:33.420
I won't tell those kids my real location.

01:06:33.740 --> 01:06:35.650
Sorry about this. They're not about to take no for an answ—

01:06:35.650 --> 01:06:38.120
Oh! You're talking to that boy?

01:06:38.120 --> 01:06:39.430
Let me, let me!

01:06:39.430 --> 01:06:41.040
Long time no see!

01:06:41.040 --> 01:06:42.790
We last spoke on the submarine?

01:06:42.790 --> 01:06:43.500
He hung up.

01:06:43.500 --> 01:06:44.430
Aww, why?

01:06:44.750 --> 01:06:46.790
He probably doesn't want to drudge up bad memories.

01:06:46.790 --> 01:06:47.710
Oh?

01:06:47.710 --> 01:06:49.560
But I didn't do anything bad…

01:06:49.560 --> 01:06:51.090
What are you doing?!

01:06:51.090 --> 01:06:52.320
How cute!

01:06:52.630 --> 01:06:55.050
Did your breasts shrink too?

01:06:55.050 --> 01:06:58.320
Or were you just as flat in your Sherry-<i>chan</i> years?

01:06:58.320 --> 01:07:00.350
It's not like that at all!

01:07:00.350 --> 01:07:02.330
They'd really be about here—

01:07:02.980 --> 01:07:05.580
No! I can't let her get to me.

01:07:05.580 --> 01:07:06.520
Hey…

01:07:06.520 --> 01:07:09.770
Why don't you join up with me and perfect that drug?

01:07:09.770 --> 01:07:13.040
Your ideal version of the Apoptoxin…

01:07:14.070 --> 01:07:16.200
And what will you do when it's perfected?

01:07:16.200 --> 01:07:19.550
Of course, first, I'll use it on myself to get back my youth!

01:07:19.870 --> 01:07:22.870
Eternal youth is every woman's dream!

01:07:22.870 --> 01:07:24.870
It would sell like hot cakes!

01:07:24.870 --> 01:07:26.710
Don't make me have to disappoint you.

01:07:27.560 --> 01:07:31.560
What I was making isn't the drug you're dreaming of.

01:07:31.880 --> 01:07:34.380
You were different when you were younger, right?

01:07:34.380 --> 01:07:42.470
Filled with greed, you used your womanly charms to make men
your toys, never looking back until you'd fulfilled your goal…

01:07:42.470 --> 01:07:45.580
That's the sort of female thief you were.

01:07:46.690 --> 01:07:48.830
When a woman lets youth get the best of her…

01:07:49.370 --> 01:07:51.480
It's the end, you know?

01:07:51.480 --> 01:07:52.830
Fujiko Mine-<i>san</i>.

01:07:54.490 --> 01:07:55.590
Right…?

01:07:55.590 --> 01:07:57.610
This bit's too small!

01:07:57.610 --> 01:07:59.410
More smoke at the front!

01:07:59.410 --> 01:08:00.590
Got it!

01:08:00.910 --> 01:08:02.700
This is great.

01:08:02.700 --> 01:08:05.350
The staff are working together more than ever.

01:08:05.660 --> 01:08:08.580
They're all surprised by how enthusiastic Emilio is.

01:08:08.580 --> 01:08:09.600
Yeah…

01:08:09.920 --> 01:08:12.190
After Japan, we'll head back to Europe.

01:08:12.500 --> 01:08:14.550
Even take a little break.

01:08:15.380 --> 01:08:17.940
Is the deal going to take place in this room?

01:08:18.400 --> 01:08:20.300
Why?

01:08:20.300 --> 01:08:22.810
Are you interested?

01:08:22.810 --> 01:08:26.950
Or is it some ridiculous sense of justice?

01:08:28.730 --> 01:08:30.710
Mouri-<i>san</i>!

01:08:31.020 --> 01:08:34.860
Sorry to ask so much of a busy detective.

01:08:34.860 --> 01:08:35.210
Oh, no.

01:08:35.860 --> 01:08:39.840
I choose my jobs based on my own values.

01:08:40.160 --> 01:08:41.530
Only one day left.

01:08:41.530 --> 01:08:43.740
I guess you won't be sleeping tonight.

01:08:43.740 --> 01:08:46.830
Oh, my part is already over.

01:08:46.830 --> 01:08:48.850
All I need to do now is drink and sleep.

01:08:49.170 --> 01:08:51.960
And I can sleep because I have such a reliable bodyguard here.

01:08:51.960 --> 01:08:54.550
You can leave Claudia-<i>san</i> in my capable hands!

01:08:54.550 --> 01:08:54.960
Clau—?!

01:08:54.960 --> 01:08:59.860
Oh, I mean, I'll make sure to guard Emilio-<i>kun</i>!

01:09:04.310 --> 01:09:06.030
Claudia-<i>san</i>?

01:09:06.770 --> 01:09:08.640
Oh, Ran-<i>san</i>.

01:09:08.640 --> 01:09:10.660
You can't relax?

01:09:11.940 --> 01:09:13.440
No…

01:09:13.440 --> 01:09:17.920
I can't relax until this stadium is
 filled with the audience tomorrow.

01:09:18.650 --> 01:09:20.800
Even though the tickets are sold out?

01:09:21.110 --> 01:09:23.200
I still get dreams.

01:09:23.200 --> 01:09:27.250
Dreams of running around the stadium all alone.

01:09:27.250 --> 01:09:28.870
Running?

01:09:28.870 --> 01:09:32.310
Sitting in all sorts of seats and trying to make an audience by myself somehow.

01:09:33.500 --> 01:09:37.060
Since I can't let Emilio find out there isn't one, I guess.

01:09:37.380 --> 01:09:39.220
Well, dreams are dreams…

01:09:39.220 --> 01:09:40.510
But it really happened.

01:09:40.510 --> 01:09:41.190
Huh?!

01:09:41.510 --> 01:09:42.430
See?

01:09:42.430 --> 01:09:46.450
They're leaving questionnaires and information about future concerts on each seat.

01:09:46.760 --> 01:09:48.640
That was my job, once.

01:09:49.680 --> 01:09:52.450
Some gigs, not even thirty people turned up.

01:09:53.220 --> 01:09:55.210
Was it hard?

01:09:55.520 --> 01:09:57.110
Of course!

01:09:57.110 --> 01:09:58.460
We didn't have any money.

01:09:59.690 --> 01:10:02.340
I felt so powerless.

01:10:02.660 --> 01:10:05.240
I couldn't do a thing for Emilio.

01:10:05.240 --> 01:10:06.530
Nothing at all…

01:10:07.200 --> 01:10:09.040
Claudia-<i>san</i>…

01:10:33.310 --> 01:10:34.500
Welcome.

01:10:35.770 --> 01:10:37.620
This place ain't changed one bit.

01:10:37.940 --> 01:10:42.450
I've got everything you asked for.

01:10:42.450 --> 01:10:44.820
Even an unused Walther?

01:10:44.820 --> 01:10:48.490
I had the grip and the spring for the trigger custom-made.

01:10:48.490 --> 01:10:50.040
It was easy.

01:10:50.040 --> 01:10:52.330
You're as good a businessman as ever.

01:10:52.330 --> 01:10:54.540
The money's in that suitcase.

01:10:54.540 --> 01:10:55.890
As for the money…

01:10:56.210 --> 01:11:00.340
Wait until you've spoken to my guest in the back.

01:11:04.970 --> 01:11:06.180
I see.

01:11:06.180 --> 01:11:08.140
So that's why I didn't even sense you.

01:11:08.140 --> 01:11:09.740
Well, I'm no ghost.

01:11:10.470 --> 01:11:12.930
Didn't think you'd still be in Japan.

01:11:12.930 --> 01:11:15.080
You already got that Sapphire, right?

01:11:15.080 --> 01:11:18.290
That's the King for you. You know about everything.

01:11:18.600 --> 01:11:22.590
Even if it's not my field, there's waves made when Lupin III gets moving.

01:11:22.940 --> 01:11:25.090
So? Why are you here?

01:11:25.450 --> 01:11:27.780
A first-class ticket to Naples.

01:11:27.780 --> 01:11:29.470
If I give you this, will you head back?

01:11:30.540 --> 01:11:31.470
You taping this or something?!

01:11:32.080 --> 01:11:34.470
There's no cameras.

01:11:34.790 --> 01:11:38.000
Give up working for Luciano.

01:11:38.000 --> 01:11:40.730
I know you didn't have any choice.

01:11:41.170 --> 01:11:43.670
But you have to stay out this time.

01:11:43.670 --> 01:11:45.480
I'm looking after you.

01:11:45.880 --> 01:11:46.850
Is it a woman?

01:11:46.850 --> 01:11:48.010
A kid.

01:11:48.890 --> 01:11:50.870
You screwed up, huh?

01:11:50.870 --> 01:11:54.810
You're <i>not</i> thinking what I'm thinking.

01:11:54.810 --> 01:11:57.700
And even if you are, I haven't ‘screwed up’.

01:11:57.700 --> 01:11:59.710
I'm not saying you should do this for free.

01:12:00.360 --> 01:12:02.480
Then what are you saying?

01:12:03.530 --> 01:12:05.420
Private photos of Yōko Okino.

01:12:07.030 --> 01:12:08.490
And…

01:12:08.490 --> 01:12:10.700
Embarrassing photos of Fujiko-<i>chan</i>.

01:12:10.700 --> 01:12:11.430
Good.

01:12:18.580 --> 01:12:20.590
All right, everyone…

01:12:20.590 --> 01:12:21.350
Here I go!

01:12:21.710 --> 01:12:22.980
I've gotta go to the toilet.

01:12:22.980 --> 01:12:24.400
Oh, oh…

01:12:23.340 --> 01:12:24.400
I should go too!

01:12:24.400 --> 01:12:28.130
Come closer… Oh, oh

01:12:24.760 --> 01:12:26.900
I'll guard him from the side of the stage.

01:12:26.900 --> 01:12:28.680
And so…

01:12:28.130 --> 01:12:31.720
Be here now… Oh, oh

01:12:28.680 --> 01:12:29.650
I'm all alone.

01:12:31.720 --> 01:12:34.700
That's good enough… Oh, oh

01:12:34.700 --> 01:12:36.810
Take you to wonderland!

01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:40.310
Love you, baby, sing together!

01:12:40.310 --> 01:12:46.440
Clap your hands until the break of dawn…

01:12:40.310 --> 01:12:41.910
Emilio!

01:12:46.440 --> 01:12:50.970
Wherever and whenever, we're feeling each other, boy!

01:12:50.970 --> 01:12:54.790
Dance in a ring, then we're together!

01:12:54.790 --> 01:13:01.000
Far in the future, and it will never change!

01:12:56.450 --> 01:12:57.810
This is strange…

01:12:57.810 --> 01:13:01.170
I haven't seen Luciano, let alone Lupin.

01:13:01.000 --> 01:13:09.180
No matter how far from you, I can feel you near!

01:13:01.170 --> 01:13:03.520
The last footage we have of Luciano is…

01:13:03.880 --> 01:13:04.960
This.

01:13:05.800 --> 01:13:07.520
This was thirty minutes ago.

01:13:07.880 --> 01:13:08.630
And where is that?

01:13:08.630 --> 01:13:12.990
It's a door that leads underground, but there
haven't been any cars leaving the parking area.

01:13:09.180 --> 01:13:14.610
I've been searching for the treasure through my life…

01:13:13.350 --> 01:13:14.610
Take a look at this.

01:13:15.810 --> 01:13:18.060
The underground tunnel has been extended!

01:13:16.180 --> 01:13:23.360
But when I began to sing there was no-one to listen to me…

01:13:18.060 --> 01:13:18.910
What is this?!

01:13:19.270 --> 01:13:21.660
Apparently it was a VIP entrance to be kept secret.

01:13:21.660 --> 01:13:23.920
We didn't find it when we searched
 the construction firm either!

01:13:23.360 --> 01:13:28.790
Now I can see the sunrise in your eyes…

01:13:29.150 --> 01:13:34.930
And I finally find this time I will let you see…

01:13:53.300 --> 01:13:54.320
Could you see me?

01:13:54.320 --> 01:13:56.610
We couldn't even see the tunnel entrance.

01:13:56.810 --> 01:13:58.100
He got us.

01:13:58.100 --> 01:13:59.870
It opens right onto a road.

01:13:59.870 --> 01:14:01.190
Wait.

01:14:01.190 --> 01:14:03.370
How about the cameras for the outdoor parking?

01:14:03.730 --> 01:14:05.540
That spot…

01:14:05.900 --> 01:14:07.110
It's no good.

01:14:07.110 --> 01:14:09.040
Your car's just out of sight.

01:14:09.400 --> 01:14:12.920
If we look back at the recording, we
might be able to tell which way he went.

01:14:13.280 --> 01:14:17.410
Back at that time, the car that went past was…

01:14:18.490 --> 01:14:19.330
What's this?!

01:14:20.160 --> 01:14:21.810
C-Conan-<i>kun</i>?!

01:14:22.160 --> 01:14:23.560
Excuse me?

01:14:28.380 --> 01:14:29.770
He won't answer.

01:14:30.070 --> 01:14:31.720
That boy…

01:14:31.720 --> 01:14:33.280
Is he always like that?

01:14:33.630 --> 01:14:36.470
He's even more focused than usual.

01:14:36.470 --> 01:14:39.070
I can't be the only one thinking that, right?

01:14:41.060 --> 01:14:41.990
Where are you going?

01:14:42.350 --> 01:14:45.440
You two keep using technology to track him.

01:14:45.440 --> 01:14:46.000
But as for me…

01:14:47.320 --> 01:14:50.380
I work best on instinct!

01:14:50.380 --> 01:14:55.700
Take you to wonderland! Love you, baby, sing together!

01:14:54.610 --> 01:14:55.990
I see.

01:14:55.700 --> 01:15:02.000
Clap your hands until the break of dawn…

01:14:55.990 --> 01:14:58.160
So he did know.

01:14:58.160 --> 01:15:02.390
But Emilio believed in you, Claudia-<i>san</i>.

01:15:02.000 --> 01:15:06.750
Whenever and wherever, we're feeling each other, boy!

01:15:02.750 --> 01:15:07.460
And he didn't want you to be involved in any more bad things…

01:15:06.750 --> 01:15:08.020
Dance in a ring, then—

01:15:08.380 --> 01:15:09.900
Let's see…

01:15:10.250 --> 01:15:12.800
Twenty <i>daikon</i>, a crate of cabbages…

01:15:12.800 --> 01:15:15.900
Ugh, they even destroyed a till…?

01:15:16.260 --> 01:15:17.220
Yes?

01:15:17.220 --> 01:15:20.030
This is Takagi, the dumb detective who
made a stupid mistake trying to arrest Lupin

01:15:20.030 --> 01:15:22.770
and got thrown off the case and made to
handle the bills of damages all by himself…

01:15:22.770 --> 01:15:24.080
What can I do for you?

01:15:24.440 --> 01:15:26.900
And I've written my apology statement already.

01:15:26.900 --> 01:15:28.190
What?

01:15:28.190 --> 01:15:29.830
Is Detective Takagi there?

01:15:30.190 --> 01:15:32.320
Oh, it's you guys!

01:15:32.320 --> 01:15:33.440
What is it?

01:15:35.150 --> 01:15:36.670
I've brought some more bills.

01:15:37.030 --> 01:15:38.780
Sorry! I'll leave them up to you!

01:15:39.060 --> 01:15:40.930
Wait, you can't do that!

01:15:41.290 --> 01:15:44.330
Detective Takagi really is the best guy to call at times like this.

01:15:44.330 --> 01:15:46.430
He always believes us!

01:15:46.790 --> 01:15:50.210
Ai-<i>chan</i>'s so mean, why'd she tell us the wrong place?

01:15:50.210 --> 01:15:55.050
No, she might have been threatened
and forced to tell us the wrong location.

01:15:55.050 --> 01:15:56.800
Let's hurry and save her!

01:15:56.800 --> 01:15:59.200
Conan-<i>kun</i> said he was gonna do something!

01:15:59.550 --> 01:16:02.390
First, let's meet up with Detective Takagi.

01:16:02.390 --> 01:16:04.230
Let's arrest 'em all!

01:16:04.230 --> 01:16:05.200
Yeah!

01:16:08.560 --> 01:16:09.520
What?

01:16:09.520 --> 01:16:12.650
Using someone else's computer
without permission is rude, you know.

01:16:12.650 --> 01:16:14.740
Giving your friends fake intel?

01:16:14.740 --> 01:16:16.840
I don't want to put them in danger.

01:16:17.320 --> 01:16:19.570
You're good at betrayal, huh?

01:16:19.570 --> 01:16:21.840
Just like how you betrayed the Organisation you were part of…

01:16:24.450 --> 01:16:26.600
But don't worry about a thing.

01:16:27.090 --> 01:16:29.600
Betrayals are like accessories for women.

01:16:29.960 --> 01:16:31.170
You're leaving?

01:16:31.170 --> 01:16:32.940
Go home if you want.

01:16:33.250 --> 01:16:39.110
But as a female thief with men as my playthings, I can't forgive the man who tricked me.

01:16:39.470 --> 01:16:40.850
Wanna come with me?

01:16:40.850 --> 01:16:42.860
It'll be super dangerous!

01:16:47.810 --> 01:16:51.120
I believe this is the first time we've met…

01:16:51.480 --> 01:16:54.130
Nice to meet you, Mr. Luciano.

01:16:54.320 --> 01:16:56.710
You can call me Alan Smithee.

01:16:57.070 --> 01:17:00.350
—near!

01:16:57.070 --> 01:16:58.400
Alan Smithee?

01:16:58.400 --> 01:17:00.630
That's who the deal's being made with?

01:17:00.350 --> 01:17:06.390
I've been searching for the treasure through my life…

01:17:00.990 --> 01:17:04.040
I heard Luciano call him that once.

01:17:04.040 --> 01:17:06.390
Did he mention where the deal was taking place?

01:17:08.120 --> 01:17:11.890
But when I began to sing, there was no-one to listen—

01:17:08.120 --> 01:17:11.890
Luciano never told anyone where it would happen.

01:17:14.890 --> 01:17:16.380
I see.

01:17:16.380 --> 01:17:18.720
You brought it to this airport as spare equipment…

01:17:18.720 --> 01:17:22.030
Here, it hasn't entered the country yet.

01:17:23.260 --> 01:17:27.680
Though even if it was checked, nobody would find anything odd about this.

01:17:33.190 --> 01:17:34.040
What's this?

01:17:34.440 --> 01:17:36.030
A keyboard?

01:17:36.030 --> 01:17:38.540
What you want…

01:17:38.940 --> 01:17:40.490
are these.

01:17:40.490 --> 01:17:42.050
It's not hard to process, right?

01:17:43.120 --> 01:17:45.430
 Well then, here's what we agreed.

01:17:47.830 --> 01:17:51.810
This is the Cherry Sapphire, as promised.

01:17:52.210 --> 01:17:53.580
A sapphire?

01:17:53.580 --> 01:17:54.730
What is that?

01:17:55.130 --> 01:17:56.630
What joke are you playing?

01:17:56.630 --> 01:17:57.980
What are you saying?

01:18:01.050 --> 01:18:06.950
Geez, you had to hide all the way out here…
You've wasted enough of my time.

01:18:11.890 --> 01:18:12.690
What?!

01:18:27.200 --> 01:18:29.250
I told you, didn't I?

01:18:29.250 --> 01:18:31.100
That I'd catch you the next time we met…

01:18:31.500 --> 01:18:33.460
This has to happen now?

01:18:33.460 --> 01:18:36.650
Didn't Daddy tell you to stop playing detective?

01:18:36.650 --> 01:18:37.710
Geez…

01:18:37.710 --> 01:18:39.710
You betrayed us?!

01:18:40.260 --> 01:18:41.610
You fired me!

01:18:42.010 --> 01:18:44.800
I'll give you a Special Last Chance…

01:18:44.800 --> 01:18:47.860
Leave now, and I'll forget you were here…

01:18:48.220 --> 01:18:49.350
You idiot.

01:18:49.350 --> 01:18:52.390
I can't just let you get away with this.

01:18:52.390 --> 01:18:54.370
You've never fired a gun, have you?

01:18:54.770 --> 01:18:58.710
Unfortunately for you, I was
 trained at a firing range in Hawaii.

01:18:59.110 --> 01:19:02.090
You tricked us! What is that jewel?!

01:19:02.950 --> 01:19:05.660
It appears that we've been set up.

01:19:05.660 --> 01:19:08.470
Have you heard of a man named Kein Gejidasu?

01:19:08.470 --> 01:19:09.850
Kein?!

01:19:09.850 --> 01:19:12.710
Who is he? I've never heard of him!

01:19:13.620 --> 01:19:15.100
Then this was my mistake?

01:19:16.420 --> 01:19:18.100
Kein Gejidasu, huh?

01:19:18.500 --> 01:19:21.800
You figured it out, deduction geek?

01:19:21.800 --> 01:19:24.480
And while we're at it, good job finding this place.

01:19:24.480 --> 01:19:26.110
You wanna know how?

01:19:26.730 --> 01:19:27.860
Later.

01:19:29.760 --> 01:19:31.370
It doesn't matter. Eliminate them.

01:19:36.310 --> 01:19:38.540
Here's a nice stage for you!

01:19:38.540 --> 01:19:39.670
Secret Sword Art!

01:19:39.670 --> 01:19:42.000
Whirlwind Blowback!{hiken tatsumakigaeshi / ref: Lupin III Part I ep 5 [21:43]}

01:19:44.570 --> 01:19:47.510
Goemon, you're making it even more dangerous!

01:19:47.990 --> 01:19:49.330
My skills are at fault.

01:19:49.330 --> 01:19:51.180
Don't go deep in thought on us now!

01:19:55.580 --> 01:19:57.100
Out of the way!

01:20:05.550 --> 01:20:07.190
I have cut…

01:20:07.680 --> 01:20:09.700
…another worthless object!

01:20:10.010 --> 01:20:11.570
I do this all the time!{very loose, but eh}

01:20:15.640 --> 01:20:16.830
Lupin! You're under arrest!

01:20:16.830 --> 01:20:19.330
The brakes aren't working!

01:20:24.440 --> 01:20:25.070
Don't move!

01:20:25.070 --> 01:20:25.710
Stay where you are!

01:20:26.110 --> 01:20:27.530
There's more of them?!

01:20:30.280 --> 01:20:33.510
Oh! Great job, Jigen, you've really improved!

01:20:33.740 --> 01:20:34.890
It wasn't me!

01:20:35.080 --> 01:20:36.930
Nor was it I.

01:20:36.930 --> 01:20:38.420
Right…

01:20:38.420 --> 01:20:39.560
Then who?

01:20:40.060 --> 01:20:41.310
Freeze!

01:20:44.930 --> 01:20:46.820
I got ya, Lupin!

01:20:47.730 --> 01:20:50.690
Jodie Starling, FBI.

01:20:50.690 --> 01:20:53.320
I'll have you come with us.

01:20:54.820 --> 01:20:56.360
A gunfight at Haneda?

01:20:56.360 --> 01:21:00.700
The old maintenance area is where private jets are kept.

01:21:00.700 --> 01:21:03.210
So they could just fly away, huh?

01:21:03.210 --> 01:21:05.240
Areas A, B, C, all clear!

01:21:06.040 --> 01:21:09.210
Knowing who we're up against, we can't let our guard down.

01:21:09.210 --> 01:21:12.590
What's the FBI doing here?

01:21:12.590 --> 01:21:14.540
I called them here.

01:21:15.210 --> 01:21:19.470
I wouldn't come here without a plan alone, now would I?

01:21:19.470 --> 01:21:21.760
Damn, I can't get in a good shot…

01:21:21.760 --> 01:21:23.730
Don't tell me he's deliberately getting in the way…

01:21:23.730 --> 01:21:27.060
We're acting on our own accord here in Japan.

01:21:27.060 --> 01:21:34.240
You've got an international arrest warrant, so if we hand you over, the Japanese police will be indebted to us.

01:21:34.550 --> 01:21:37.360
Jodie-<i>kun</i>, cuff him.

01:21:37.360 --> 01:21:38.240
Gotcha!

01:21:38.240 --> 01:21:39.570
Come along peacefully now.

01:21:39.570 --> 01:21:40.620
Sure!

01:21:42.500 --> 01:21:43.910
Wait!

01:21:43.910 --> 01:21:46.030
Don't touch him without checking.

01:21:46.030 --> 01:21:48.420
You don't know what he's got hidden up his sleeves.

01:21:48.920 --> 01:21:50.960
What a brat…

01:21:50.960 --> 01:21:54.580
Put your hands behind your head,
 and get down on your knees.

01:21:54.580 --> 01:21:55.470
Right, right…

01:21:55.890 --> 01:22:00.220
I'll put him to sleep first, just to be sure…

01:22:00.220 --> 01:22:02.720
You really are an annoying brat…

01:22:20.360 --> 01:22:20.990
Damn you!

01:22:20.990 --> 01:22:21.870
Stop!

01:22:24.740 --> 01:22:27.320
If you want to shoot me, then fire away.

01:22:27.320 --> 01:22:28.780
But…

01:22:28.780 --> 01:22:31.750
Even if you shoot straight through my head…

01:22:32.380 --> 01:22:35.260
I <i>will</i> pull this trigger.

01:22:35.670 --> 01:22:37.750
Give me back that case.

01:22:39.010 --> 01:22:39.760
Here.

01:22:40.340 --> 01:22:42.760
All units, stay where you are.

01:22:43.510 --> 01:22:46.470
Would you move away from me, if you could?

01:22:49.850 --> 01:22:51.520
Don't make me shoot the child!

01:22:51.520 --> 01:22:54.530
Got it, I'm cool, I'm going…

01:22:54.530 --> 01:22:57.530
Wasn't this your big chance, little brat?

01:23:01.190 --> 01:23:02.780
Oh, Alan-<i>san</i>!

01:23:02.780 --> 01:23:04.360
What about the money you promised?

01:23:04.360 --> 01:23:06.290
Weren't you going to trade it for money?

01:23:06.290 --> 01:23:07.870
Pilot, can you hear me?

01:23:07.870 --> 01:23:08.490
Yes.

01:23:08.490 --> 01:23:10.240
Start the engines. We leave immediately.

01:23:10.240 --> 01:23:11.200
Roger.

01:23:11.200 --> 01:23:12.330
Bring the case.

01:23:12.330 --> 01:23:14.000
The money's over in the car.

01:23:14.000 --> 01:23:15.210
Bring the car!

01:23:15.210 --> 01:23:17.010
Y-Yes, sir!

01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:22.050
This is Satō!

01:23:22.050 --> 01:23:23.180
We'll be there in three minutes!

01:23:23.180 --> 01:23:25.060
Open the gate!

01:23:25.060 --> 01:23:27.340
W-Why are you here, Takagi-<i>kun</i>?!

01:23:27.340 --> 01:23:29.190
T-This is bad!

01:23:29.190 --> 01:23:30.550
Don't let 'em beat you, Doc!

01:23:30.550 --> 01:23:32.390
They're getting ahead of us!

01:23:32.390 --> 01:23:34.810
We've got Detective Takagi with us!

01:23:34.810 --> 01:23:35.700
Okay!

01:23:35.700 --> 01:23:37.940
This is really bad!

01:23:37.940 --> 01:23:40.700
Non-police vehicles should clear the way!

01:23:44.620 --> 01:23:46.110
Where's your car?

01:23:46.110 --> 01:23:49.200
You think we'd sneak up on you in a car?

01:23:49.200 --> 01:23:50.920
I've just asked for a helicopter.

01:23:50.920 --> 01:23:53.000
They're getting away…

01:23:56.080 --> 01:23:57.630
T-They're gonna shoot us, aren't they?!

01:23:57.630 --> 01:23:59.460
Drop the gun.

01:23:59.460 --> 01:24:01.000
They won't shoot.

01:24:01.000 --> 01:24:01.920
Drive!

01:24:01.920 --> 01:24:03.550
Get ready to take off.

01:24:03.550 --> 01:24:05.140
Ignore air traffic control.

01:24:07.550 --> 01:24:10.140
My cute little Alfa Romeo…

01:24:10.140 --> 01:24:12.680
What should we do? Run after them?

01:24:12.680 --> 01:24:13.890
What can we do?

01:24:13.890 --> 01:24:15.150
Lupin!

01:24:15.150 --> 01:24:16.690
Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

01:24:16.690 --> 01:24:17.460
Who's that?

01:24:17.460 --> 01:24:18.440
Fujiko Mine.

01:24:18.440 --> 01:24:22.150
Bust: 99, Waist: 55, Hips: 88.

01:24:22.150 --> 01:24:25.480
She's also wanted worldwide.

01:24:27.200 --> 01:24:29.040
It's all over?

01:24:29.040 --> 01:24:32.040
No way! We're just getting started.

01:24:37.710 --> 01:24:40.790
Lupin and the FBI…

01:24:40.790 --> 01:24:43.680
They both stood down to protect you…

01:24:43.680 --> 01:24:47.170
Kid, just who are you?

01:24:59.070 --> 01:25:01.360
Why am I the one driving?!

01:25:01.360 --> 01:25:03.360
You'd rather fire then?

01:25:03.360 --> 01:25:05.270
Don't worry, this'll be over soon enough!

01:25:05.270 --> 01:25:07.150
H-Hey, wait, Fujiko-<i>chan</i>!

01:25:07.150 --> 01:25:08.860
The brat's in there!

01:25:08.860 --> 01:25:10.370
Doesn't matter to me.

01:25:10.370 --> 01:25:14.630
If you try and shoot him, I'll turn the bike and crash it first.

01:25:14.630 --> 01:25:18.250
Then how about telling me the secret behind that drug?

01:25:20.410 --> 01:25:21.670
Fine.

01:25:21.670 --> 01:25:23.000
Then let's get rid of these!

01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:24.380
You just threw them away?!

01:25:24.380 --> 01:25:25.550
I'll use these instead.

01:25:25.550 --> 01:25:27.050
Speed it up!

01:25:27.500 --> 01:25:29.060
Raise your foot!

01:25:30.920 --> 01:25:32.930
Oh my, Sherry-<i>chan</i>…

01:25:32.930 --> 01:25:35.550
I used to ride a Harley too.

01:25:35.550 --> 01:25:36.440
You got a problem with that?

01:25:38.940 --> 01:25:41.230
Don't take your eyes off that child.

01:25:41.230 --> 01:25:41.690
Yes, sir!

01:25:43.940 --> 01:25:45.150
Everything's fine.

01:25:45.150 --> 01:25:45.860
Take off.

01:25:45.860 --> 01:25:47.700
They won't stop complaining…

01:25:47.700 --> 01:25:48.860
GB27!

01:25:48.860 --> 01:25:50.360
Stop immediately!

01:25:50.360 --> 01:25:51.950
Another plane is approaching!

01:25:51.950 --> 01:25:55.460
JNA301! Abort landing!

01:25:51.990 --> 01:25:55.460
GB27! GB27!

01:26:01.710 --> 01:26:03.710
Don't tell me you intend to…

01:26:03.710 --> 01:26:05.340
I'll stop them by force if I have to!

01:26:05.750 --> 01:26:08.180
I should've stayed behind!

01:26:08.750 --> 01:26:10.050
We're at V1.

01:26:10.050 --> 01:26:11.090
Take off!

01:26:17.020 --> 01:26:17.810
We're gonna fly!

01:26:37.170 --> 01:26:38.280
Raise landing gear.

01:26:38.280 --> 01:26:40.040
Raising landing gear.

01:26:40.040 --> 01:26:42.870
JNA pilot, can you hear me?

01:26:42.870 --> 01:26:43.910
Stay on course.

01:26:43.910 --> 01:26:45.300
We'll avoid you.

01:26:53.590 --> 01:26:55.760
Get ambulances to the old maintenance area!

01:26:55.760 --> 01:26:57.350
There are many people injured!

01:26:57.350 --> 01:26:59.390
Why won't they let us in?!

01:26:59.390 --> 01:27:00.890
I guess there's nothing we can do…

01:27:00.890 --> 01:27:02.890
We've got a detective in here!

01:27:02.890 --> 01:27:04.360
Don't keep saying that…

01:27:04.360 --> 01:27:06.440
Make them let us through, Takagi!

01:27:05.060 --> 01:27:06.440
What a relief!

01:27:06.440 --> 01:27:07.810
Make them?!

01:27:06.440 --> 01:27:07.810
So you're okay, Ai-<i>chan</i>?

01:27:07.810 --> 01:27:09.190
Show them your police badge!

01:27:09.190 --> 01:27:09.870
Right.

01:27:10.550 --> 01:27:13.620
Conan-<i>kun</i>'s riding a <i>what</i>?!

01:27:17.110 --> 01:27:19.620
Agh… What sort of piloting was that?!

01:27:19.620 --> 01:27:23.580
Honestly! I almost fell off!

01:27:23.580 --> 01:27:25.130
What?!

01:27:30.140 --> 01:27:32.630
You sure do a lot, brat.

01:27:34.640 --> 01:27:37.010
I'll end up losing my patience.

01:27:37.010 --> 01:27:38.640
What were you thinking?

01:27:38.640 --> 01:27:39.390
What do you mean?

01:27:39.390 --> 01:27:40.440
Don't play dumb with me…

01:27:40.440 --> 01:27:43.690
There weren't any fatalities in that huge gunfight…

01:27:43.690 --> 01:27:49.200
That means you're the one who
 positioned those FBI agents, right?

01:27:49.200 --> 01:27:54.200
Always thinking about the power balance, so there wouldn't be any fatal wounds…

01:27:55.300 --> 01:27:56.780
What a pain!

01:27:56.780 --> 01:28:00.620
If they'd wiped each other out,
 it'd be case closed for us!

01:28:00.620 --> 01:28:02.330
And that's what you were aiming for!

01:28:02.330 --> 01:28:04.840
Yeah! And it was going so well!

01:28:04.840 --> 01:28:07.000
Gonna leave the last act up to me?

01:28:07.670 --> 01:28:11.040
Don't resent me if it doesn't go as you planned.

01:28:12.790 --> 01:28:15.600
We've finally got it, Captain…

01:28:15.600 --> 01:28:16.800
Yes…

01:28:16.800 --> 01:28:19.640
Now Girambar will be able to fight too.

01:28:32.860 --> 01:28:35.440
Oh my, somebody's hard-headed!

01:28:36.620 --> 01:28:37.830
You idiot!

01:28:45.340 --> 01:28:46.420
Give it up!

01:28:46.420 --> 01:28:48.420
He dug his own grave.

01:28:57.310 --> 01:29:00.230
Don't go ending this contest in a tie now…

01:29:02.890 --> 01:29:05.510
We're okay. I can smell the sea breeze.

01:29:05.510 --> 01:29:07.560
It's a surprise that we haven't crashed.

01:29:07.560 --> 01:29:09.400
Looks like there's still someone to thank.

01:29:15.280 --> 01:29:18.110
Good job staying in control this far…

01:29:18.110 --> 01:29:19.240
I'll take over.

01:29:21.290 --> 01:29:23.870
The throttle's still okay…

01:29:23.870 --> 01:29:27.350
The tail fin control's heavy…

01:29:27.350 --> 01:29:28.540
Okay, got it.

01:29:28.540 --> 01:29:29.630
Brat?

01:29:29.630 --> 01:29:31.040
Oil pressure's at zero.

01:29:31.040 --> 01:29:33.260
This plane has a backup, right?

01:29:33.570 --> 01:29:39.140
You really are a surprise. Just who are you?

01:29:39.140 --> 01:29:41.430
Don't strain yourself. He's—

01:29:41.430 --> 01:29:43.020
Shin'ichi Kudō.

01:29:43.020 --> 01:29:45.400
A high-school detective.

01:29:45.400 --> 01:29:47.350
A high-schooler?

01:29:48.600 --> 01:29:51.710
You still have…

01:29:51.710 --> 01:29:52.990
…the potential…

01:29:53.560 --> 01:29:54.520
…to do anything.

01:29:55.650 --> 01:29:57.480
Even in my country…

01:29:58.190 --> 01:29:59.780
…lots of…

01:29:59.780 --> 01:30:00.440
…kids…

01:30:02.240 --> 01:30:07.490
His country's being treated as
 a colony by a neighbouring country.

01:30:07.490 --> 01:30:09.700
With overwhelming military force…

01:30:10.870 --> 01:30:13.760
What's his real name?

01:30:13.760 --> 01:30:15.670
Isn't Alan Smithee a fake name?

01:30:15.670 --> 01:30:17.130
What's it matter?

01:30:17.130 --> 01:30:18.840
Let him be Alan Smithee.

01:30:19.760 --> 01:30:21.560
Orders to shoot it down?!

01:30:21.560 --> 01:30:24.300
It's apparently direct from the ambassador of Girambar.

01:30:24.300 --> 01:30:27.930
But there's a boy aboard the plane!

01:30:27.930 --> 01:30:30.940
Connect me to Superintendant Matsumoto!

01:30:32.520 --> 01:30:34.820
We can make it to Hachijōjima Island.

01:30:34.820 --> 01:30:37.770
Why not return to Haneda and give yourself up?

01:30:37.770 --> 01:30:39.360
The FBI's there.

01:30:39.360 --> 01:30:40.830
Don't be silly.

01:30:40.830 --> 01:30:42.570
You know…

01:30:42.570 --> 01:30:44.960
If you shoot that, we'll crash.

01:30:44.960 --> 01:30:47.370
I can pilot this fine by myself.

01:30:47.370 --> 01:30:48.330
Don't underestimate this.

01:30:48.330 --> 01:30:51.080
Even I'm belted in and doing everything I can.

01:30:51.080 --> 01:30:53.250
Hurry up and get the comms and radar working!

01:30:53.250 --> 01:30:54.460
Right, right…

01:30:54.890 --> 01:30:56.790
If I fix this…

01:30:56.790 --> 01:30:58.840
Will you report in to Vespania?

01:31:01.460 --> 01:31:04.270
That's an interesting thing to say.

01:31:04.270 --> 01:31:05.840
When did you realise?

01:31:05.840 --> 01:31:11.410
I found out early on that the deal involved Vespanian ore.

01:31:11.410 --> 01:31:16.230
Jigen was holding dowsing rods back at the hotel.

01:31:16.230 --> 01:31:20.030
He was looking for Vespanian ore with those, right?

01:31:20.030 --> 01:31:22.900
He showed them to me back in Vespania.

01:31:22.900 --> 01:31:24.540
Now why'd he have to do that…?

01:31:24.540 --> 01:31:28.200
That isn't enough evidence to tell
 it's Vespanian ore though, is it?

01:31:28.200 --> 01:31:29.540
Oh, and then…

01:31:29.540 --> 01:31:34.050
When he opened the case, you
checked that they were the real thing.

01:31:34.050 --> 01:31:35.330
Who did?

01:31:35.330 --> 01:31:36.720
And how?

01:31:36.720 --> 01:31:39.720
Daisuke Jigen hit it with microwaves.

01:31:39.720 --> 01:31:42.890
He didn't use much power, but
you even turned the lights off…

01:31:42.890 --> 01:31:44.890
Will you tell me how it started?

01:31:44.890 --> 01:31:46.300
Sure…

01:31:46.300 --> 01:31:49.890
This may be your last deduction, after all…

01:31:51.400 --> 01:31:53.810
That was hardly a deduction at all…

01:31:53.810 --> 01:31:55.890
Just child's play…

01:31:55.890 --> 01:32:00.160
The man who was storing the Cherry
Sapphire at that bank, Eishin Wakagomo…

01:32:00.160 --> 01:32:03.650
And the man mentioned earlier during the deal…

01:32:03.650 --> 01:32:06.540
Have you heard of a man named Kein Gejidasu?

01:32:06.540 --> 01:32:07.780
Kein?!

01:32:07.780 --> 01:32:08.960
Who is he?

01:32:08.960 --> 01:32:12.080
Eishin Wakagomo is Goemon Ishikawa.

01:32:12.080 --> 01:32:16.710
And Kein Gejidasu is Daisuke Jigen. They're anagrams.

01:32:16.710 --> 01:32:19.500
Couldn't you come up with anything better?

01:32:19.500 --> 01:32:23.040
Even the Detective Boys figured out Eishin Wakagomo!

01:32:23.040 --> 01:32:26.970
Thanks to that, they headed to
 your hideout full of confidence…

01:32:26.970 --> 01:32:28.480
You don't have to say it like that…

01:32:28.480 --> 01:32:32.350
Jigen and Goemon tried their hardest to come up with those names…

01:32:32.350 --> 01:32:38.860
That means that you went out of your way to steal the Cherry Sapphire that Goemon left at the bank.

01:32:38.860 --> 01:32:46.370
And Daisuke Jigen, disguised as Kein Gejidasu, told Alan that the deal would take place for the Cherry Sapphire.

01:32:46.370 --> 01:32:48.870
And the thief he recommended to steal it…

01:32:48.870 --> 01:32:51.750
…was Lupin III.

01:32:51.750 --> 01:33:01.260
In other words, your goal was never the Cherry Sapphire, but to get close to Alan, who was after the stolen Vespanian ore,

01:33:01.260 --> 01:33:09.270
figure out who he was trying to buy it from, and then steal it right back to profit.

01:33:09.270 --> 01:33:15.510
If the Cherry Sapphire was yours to begin with, you would've put a transmitter in it for sure.

01:33:15.510 --> 01:33:20.280
I picked up the signal with these, and that's how I found where the deal would happen.

01:33:20.580 --> 01:33:25.410
And let me guess, Fujiko Mine probably
befriended him to try and steal back the ore?

01:33:25.410 --> 01:33:29.700
The ore being stolen is all over the net, too.

01:33:29.700 --> 01:33:30.900
You idiot.

01:33:30.900 --> 01:33:35.910
Stealing back some stolen rock
 ain't even gonna get me one yen.

01:33:35.910 --> 01:33:39.590
But you <i>did</i> try and steal it back.

01:33:39.590 --> 01:33:41.290
Now why would that be?

01:33:41.290 --> 01:33:42.420
Who knows?

01:33:42.420 --> 01:33:44.090
We're not playing twenty questions here!

01:33:44.090 --> 01:33:45.590
The answer is…

01:33:47.210 --> 01:33:53.100
Because it was the Vespanian ore which the late Queen Sakura gave her life for.

01:33:54.140 --> 01:34:00.520
It was probably that tomboy daughter of hers that asked you to do it.

01:34:00.520 --> 01:34:04.690
But you know, if you just figured out the thief was Luciano a bit earlier,

01:34:04.690 --> 01:34:08.370
you wouldn't have had to come to
Japan and have that gunfight, right?

01:34:08.860 --> 01:34:11.780
Guess I let my guard down slightly.

01:34:11.780 --> 01:34:15.670
I wanted to meet a certain cheeky
 brat of a Great Detective here.

01:34:18.080 --> 01:34:19.540
Whatever…

01:34:20.010 --> 01:34:22.580
Okay, this should work for now.

01:34:22.580 --> 01:34:23.800
Thank you!

01:34:25.180 --> 01:34:26.960
You know how this goes.

01:34:26.960 --> 01:34:29.550
You know too much…

01:34:29.550 --> 01:34:32.920
Perceptions are important in this line of work.

01:34:32.920 --> 01:34:35.300
Lupin III doesn't rescue people.

01:34:35.300 --> 01:34:39.560
If that was supposed to be a joke, you could've at least taken the safety off your Walther.

01:34:39.560 --> 01:34:40.860
That spoilt the whole thing.

01:34:44.570 --> 01:34:46.480
Eagle One to Command HQ!

01:34:46.480 --> 01:34:49.450
Final code, 1027, confirm!

01:34:49.450 --> 01:34:51.700
Final code confirmed.

01:34:49.450 --> 01:34:51.700
Air Defence Direction Centre

01:34:51.700 --> 01:34:54.070
You have permission to fire your missiles.

01:34:54.070 --> 01:34:57.210
I repeat, you have permission to fire your missiles.

01:34:57.210 --> 01:34:59.460
Royal orders from Vespania?!

01:34:59.460 --> 01:35:02.200
If the worst happens and I don't get it back…

01:35:03.000 --> 01:35:04.460
If you don't…?

01:35:04.460 --> 01:35:07.080
Before it can be taken out of Japan…

01:35:07.080 --> 01:35:08.220
Destroy it.

01:35:08.220 --> 01:35:10.550
You should've planned for this!

01:35:10.550 --> 01:35:12.130
Well, you weren't in my plans!

01:35:12.130 --> 01:35:15.550
With you disguised as Kid, did you
expect me to sit back and do nothing?!

01:35:15.550 --> 01:35:17.100
Can't you take a joke?!

01:35:19.480 --> 01:35:20.680
Here it comes!

01:35:20.680 --> 01:35:21.990
Full throttle!

01:35:23.980 --> 01:35:25.230
We've got chaff!

01:35:25.230 --> 01:35:26.110
Fire it!

01:35:30.240 --> 01:35:31.400
This is the Girambar plane!

01:35:31.400 --> 01:35:33.450
To the Eagle attacking us—!

01:35:34.370 --> 01:35:36.820
Target launched chaff to intercept attack.

01:35:36.820 --> 01:35:38.370
Attack did not land.

01:35:38.370 --> 01:35:42.870
We have orders from both the Kingdom of Vespania and the Republic of Girambar.

01:35:42.870 --> 01:35:44.800
Use the AM-10!

01:35:44.800 --> 01:35:46.130
Roger!

01:35:46.130 --> 01:35:47.970
The next one will finish us off!

01:35:47.970 --> 01:35:49.790
We don't have any way to block it!

01:35:50.640 --> 01:35:52.710
That's the Cherry Sapphire.

01:35:52.710 --> 01:35:55.390
I made it by shaving down a certain pebble!

01:35:55.390 --> 01:35:56.740
This?

01:35:59.180 --> 01:36:01.150
A pebble? You don't mean…!

01:36:01.150 --> 01:36:02.140
Yeah!

01:36:02.140 --> 01:36:03.850
You saw Fujiko with it before…

01:36:03.850 --> 01:36:05.650
It's Vespanian ore!

01:36:07.650 --> 01:36:09.480
The high-voltage panel in the hold!

01:36:09.480 --> 01:36:10.490
Got it!

01:36:10.490 --> 01:36:12.940
Stealth isn't its only use.

01:36:12.940 --> 01:36:16.290
When a certain voltage passes through it, it can nullify all electric devices.

01:36:16.290 --> 01:36:20.250
If a military state got their hands on it…

01:36:20.250 --> 01:36:23.130
The world's military balance would collapse!

01:36:23.130 --> 01:36:24.750
Is that it?

01:36:36.100 --> 01:36:37.840
What's wrong, brat?!

01:36:37.840 --> 01:36:38.850
Hurry it up!

01:36:38.850 --> 01:36:40.480
Not good…

01:36:44.480 --> 01:36:46.570
They've locked onto us!

01:36:46.570 --> 01:36:47.980
Head up!

01:36:47.980 --> 01:36:49.940
Then do a zero-gravity dive!

01:36:49.940 --> 01:36:52.200
So that's your plan!

01:37:00.030 --> 01:37:01.910
Hold on, brat!

01:37:07.090 --> 01:37:08.800
Just a bit more…

01:37:08.800 --> 01:37:10.420
There's only gonna be…

01:37:12.430 --> 01:37:13.800
Now!

01:37:23.690 --> 01:37:24.940
…one chance!

01:37:35.860 --> 01:37:36.940
I-I've lost control!

01:37:36.940 --> 01:37:37.830
What's going on?

01:37:39.780 --> 01:37:41.320
Abort!

01:37:41.320 --> 01:37:43.710
Eagle One, can you hear me?! Abort!

01:37:43.710 --> 01:37:45.450
There is a civilian aboard!

01:37:45.450 --> 01:37:47.710
Abort the plan immediately!

01:37:50.460 --> 01:37:52.290
This is Eagle One. Roger!

01:37:52.290 --> 01:37:56.800
But the target is falling with a mysterious light!

01:38:14.230 --> 01:38:15.610
A boat?!

01:38:17.530 --> 01:38:19.480
This is Eagle One!

01:38:19.480 --> 01:38:20.610
Parachute sighted!

01:38:20.610 --> 01:38:21.790
I can see them!

01:38:21.790 --> 01:38:25.540
Parachute confirmed at point 0925!

01:38:29.200 --> 01:38:30.920
They spotted us…

01:38:31.410 --> 01:38:33.300
They're not gonna shoot.

01:38:33.300 --> 01:38:36.420
So what next, the JMSDF?!

01:38:36.420 --> 01:38:38.260
You got the FBI involved, after all!

01:38:38.260 --> 01:38:40.760
I hardly did a thing…

01:38:40.760 --> 01:38:43.090
No, I can't believe you!

01:38:43.090 --> 01:38:45.010
You should fall off, you brat!

01:38:43.260 --> 01:38:45.550
Stop that!

01:38:45.550 --> 01:38:46.550
Ow! My arm's injured!

01:38:46.550 --> 01:38:48.270
Take that! You squid! You octopus!

01:39:00.070 --> 01:39:01.730
Encore!

01:39:01.730 --> 01:39:02.580
Encore!

01:39:07.230 --> 01:39:08.450
Were you watching?

01:39:09.800 --> 01:39:11.910
Yes. You were wonderful.

01:39:13.550 --> 01:39:16.840
Will you stay with me, and never stop watching me?

01:39:18.590 --> 01:39:20.140
Turn around.

01:39:21.250 --> 01:39:24.140
You belong out there.

01:39:27.890 --> 01:39:29.150
Let's go!

01:39:31.970 --> 01:39:34.140
Is that so? Glad to hear it.

01:39:35.150 --> 01:39:37.100
Inspector…

01:39:37.100 --> 01:39:41.410
Thank you for letting me watch
through to the end of the show.

01:39:42.030 --> 01:39:44.790
Oh, did you need something?

01:39:44.790 --> 01:39:46.070
What…?

01:39:46.790 --> 01:39:48.240
Aww…

01:39:48.240 --> 01:39:50.990
And the treasure rests at the bottom of the sea.

01:39:50.990 --> 01:39:52.790
I hate when things end like this.

01:39:54.550 --> 01:39:58.800
That big grin on your face gives me the creeps.

01:39:58.800 --> 01:40:02.090
And you're not grinning at all then?

01:40:02.090 --> 01:40:04.050
You make me smile…

01:40:04.050 --> 01:40:06.720
To see you doing something for someone else…

01:40:06.720 --> 01:40:11.810
It's like a thief has picked open a door somewhere deep in your heart…

01:40:11.810 --> 01:40:13.010
You idiot…

01:40:18.650 --> 01:40:20.560
N-Not this submarine!

01:40:21.480 --> 01:40:23.570
Bring back bad memories?

01:40:27.150 --> 01:40:29.660
Hi! How've you been, little boy?

01:40:30.410 --> 01:40:33.250
Hey, did something really happen to you?

01:40:33.560 --> 01:40:36.540
Ugh, I hate cramped spaces.

01:40:36.540 --> 01:40:38.040
I must agree.

01:40:38.040 --> 01:40:40.500
You really don't give in.

01:40:40.500 --> 01:40:42.930
Haibara! You're here too?

01:40:42.930 --> 01:40:44.670
And just what do you mean by that?

01:40:44.670 --> 01:40:47.760
If I wasn't here for you, you'd be ash back at Haneda!

01:40:47.760 --> 01:40:48.970
That's right.

01:40:48.970 --> 01:40:51.940
I would've shot you if she hadn't agreed to my little request.

01:40:51.940 --> 01:40:53.100
Request?

01:40:53.100 --> 01:40:55.570
My, what could you mean?

01:40:55.570 --> 01:40:56.640
Hey!

01:40:56.640 --> 01:40:58.320
Don't tell me you're betraying me?!

01:40:58.320 --> 01:41:01.320
Betrayals are like accessories for women.

01:41:01.320 --> 01:41:02.440
Isn't that right?

01:41:05.230 --> 01:41:08.860
Oh, my!

01:45:16.580 --> 01:45:17.650
Emilio!

01:45:17.650 --> 01:45:19.580
Come back anytime!{lol, Emirio}

01:45:21.910 --> 01:45:25.330
Thank you, Conan Edogawa.

01:45:25.330 --> 01:45:30.830
Even after all that happened, he still has so many fans cheering for him.

01:45:30.830 --> 01:45:32.340
I'm sure he'll be fine.

01:45:32.340 --> 01:45:36.510
That's right, what do you think
 Lupin's gang are up to about now?

01:45:37.630 --> 01:45:39.660
Who knows?

01:45:39.660 --> 01:45:43.770
He's probably off chasing another treasure in some faraway country.

01:45:48.520 --> 01:45:51.030
Thief dropping in!

01:45:51.030 --> 01:45:52.940
How naïve!

01:45:52.940 --> 01:45:58.280
There's no way I'd leave Japan
emptyhanded after coming all the way here!

01:45:59.240 --> 01:46:00.320
What's this?

01:46:00.320 --> 01:46:02.470
Where's the treasure?

01:46:02.790 --> 01:46:04.420
‘My apologies.’

01:46:04.420 --> 01:46:05.420
‘—Kaitō Kid.’

01:46:06.830 --> 01:46:09.090
You're under arrest, Lupin!

01:46:09.090 --> 01:46:11.540
No way!

01:46:11.540 --> 01:46:12.840
You're not getting away!

01:46:12.840 --> 01:46:16.170
It wasn't me! You've gotta believe me, Pops!

01:46:16.170 --> 01:46:18.550
Who'd ever believe <i>you</i>?!

01:46:18.550 --> 01:46:20.510
Damn you!

01:46:20.510 --> 01:46:22.130
I'll remember this, Kid!

01:46:22.130 --> 01:46:24.270
You'll get what's coming to you…

01:46:29.640 --> 01:46:31.780
You've got to be kidding me.
